COLLDATA("tadabburen","en",[[64,"§Al-Imran\ndeeds\nEngage today in enjoining what is right and forbidding what is wrong.\nRecall a sin that you take lightly, and keep away from it so that you do not fall into humiliation and destitution.\nShare a message in which you warn against harming scholars and righteous people, as they are the heirs of the Prophets.\nguid\nRemember that the goodness of this Muslim nation comes from enjoining what is right, forbidding what is wrong, and believing in Allah.\nBeing fair in judging groups and individuals is commanded by Sharia.\nWhen fighting starts, the weakness of the enemy is exposed.\nrefl\nكُنتُمۡ خَيۡرَ أُمَّةٍ أُخۡرِجَتۡ لِلنَّاسِ تَأۡمُرُونَ بِٱلۡمَعۡرُوفِ وَتَنۡهَوۡنَ عَنِ ٱلۡمُنكَرِ\nWhoever likes to be among this praised Ummah (Muslims), let him fulfill Allah's condition for it. Those from this Ummah who do not have these qualities are similar to the people of the Scriptures whom Allah condemned by saying: (They did not forbid one another from the evil which they committed) [5:79]. Ibn Kathir: 1/374.\nThe verse mentions an advantage for Muslims over other nations. What is it?\nكُنتُمۡ خَيۡرَ أُمَّةٍ أُخۡرِجَتۡ لِلنَّاسِ تَأۡمُرُونَ بِٱلۡمَعۡرُوفِ وَتَنۡهَوۡنَ عَنِ ٱلۡمُنكَرِ وَتُؤۡمِنُونَ بِٱللَّهِۗ\nThe word (right) denotes everything that is good and likable by the believers who know that obedience to Allah is the right thing to do. The word (wrong) denotes everything that is bad and abhorred by Allah and the believers who condemn it because it is disobedience to Allah. Al-Tabari: 7/105.\nWhat is meant by (right)? And what is meant by (wrong)?\nكُنتُمۡ خَيۡرَ أُمَّةٍ أُخۡرِجَتۡ لِلنَّاسِ تَأۡمُرُونَ بِٱلۡمَعۡرُوفِ وَتَنۡهَوۡنَ عَنِ ٱلۡمُنكَرِ\nJihad against the disbelievers is better than their demise by a punishment from Allah for several reasons. First: It is more rewarding for the believers due to their Jihad in the cause of Allah to make His Word supreme and the religion is entirely for Him. Second: It is more beneficial for the disbelievers themselves because some may embrace Islam, and the young ones among them who are taken captive may also become Muslim. This meaning comes from this verse: (You are the best nation ever raised for mankind). Abu Hurairah (t) said: \"You are the best of peoples for mankind, as you bring them with chains and shackles until they enter Paradise.\" Thus, this nation is the best nation ever raised for mankind. Ibn Taimyah: 2/122.\nMuslims' Jihad against the disbelievers is part of being the best nation. Explain.\nضُرِبَتۡ عَلَيۡهِمُ ٱلذِّلَّةُ أَيۡنَ مَا ثُقِفُوٓاْ إِلَّا بِحَبۡلٖ مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ وَحَبۡلٖ مِّنَ ٱلنَّاسِ وَبَآءُو بِغَضَبٖ مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ وَضُرِبَتۡ عَلَيۡهِمُ ٱلۡمَسۡكَنَةُۚ\nAfter disclosing their humiliation, Allah states that He will treat them in a manner contrary to what they want at all times and in all places. For their greed for leadership, they are afflicted with humiliation; for their attachment to wealth, they are afflicted with destitution. This punishment will be like a permanent collar for them, remaining in their descendants. Al-Biqai: 2/136.\nJews are punished with humiliation and destitution for two sins. What were they?\nوَيَقۡتُلُونَ ٱلۡأَنۢبِيَآءَ بِغَيۡرِ حَقّٖۚ\nMeaning: They responded to the Prophets of Allah, who showed them the greatest kindness, in the most evil of ways, by killing them. After such an audacious crime, could there be anything worse than that? Al-Saadi: 143.\nResponding adversely to reformers is a recurring habit of corruptors. Explain in light of this verse.\nلَيۡسُواْ سَوَآءٗۗ مِّنۡ أَهۡلِ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ أُمَّةٞ قَآئِمَةٞ يَتۡلُونَ ءَايَٰتِ ٱللَّهِ ءَانَآءَ ٱلَّيۡلِ وَهُمۡ يَسۡجُدُونَ ١١٣\nStaying up at night to study and seek knowledge for the sake of Allah is also included in this verse, and it is better than performing voluntary prayers for one whose knowledge may be beneficial to Muslims. Ibn Atiyah: 1/493.\nWhen is studying knowledge at night better than performing voluntary prayers?\nوَيَأۡمُرُونَ بِٱلۡمَعۡرُوفِ وَيَنۡهَوۡنَ عَنِ ٱلۡمُنكَرِ وَيُسَٰرِعُونَ فِي ٱلۡخَيۡرَٰتِۖ وَأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ مِنَ ٱلصَّٰلِحِينَ ١١٤\n(And hasten to good deeds), that is, they hasten to do good deeds and acts of obedience in fear of failing to do so before death. Or, they do good deeds willingly and with determination, knowing their great rewards and good consequences. This trait (rushing to good deeds) is inclusive of all kinds of virtue and excellence, and it is mentioned to allude to the Jews' slowness and hesitation in doing so.. Al-Alusi: 4/34.\nWhat prompted the believers to hasten to do good deeds?\nwords\nثُقِفُواWherever they may be\nبِحَبلٍBy a covenant\nالمَسكَنَةُDestitution\nفَلَن يُكفَرُوهُTheir reward will never be denied"],[65,"§Al-Imran\ndeeds\nWrite a message about the wealth and appearances of polytheists and the fact that these things will not benefit them.\nToday, evaluate your companions; bring close those who help you worship Allah, and replace those who distance you from the remembrance of Allah.\nCongratulate a Muslim who receives a blessing, and console another who faces hardships because that is a trait of a true believer.\nguid\nSins are the cause of calamities.\nA wise Muslim seeks advice only from sincere believers.\nAlways remember that victory over the enemies and safety from their plots are contingent upon the fear of Allah and patience.\nrefl\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ لَا تَتَّخِذُواْ بِطَانَةٗ مِّن دُونِكُمۡ لَا يَأۡلُونَكُمۡ خَبَالٗا وَدُّواْ مَا عَنِتُّمۡ قَدۡ بَدَتِ ٱلۡبَغۡضَآءُ مِنۡ أَفۡوَٰهِهِمۡ وَمَا تُخۡفِي صُدُورُهُمۡ أَكۡبَرُۚ\nIt is a forbidden to take the disbelievers as confidants. It was said to Omar Ibn Al-Khattab (t): \" There is a man here who is a Christian, and no one has better handwriting than him, will you let him write for you?\" Omar replied: \"Then I will take as a confidant from among those other than the believers.\" (They spare no effort to ruin you), meaning: They will do everything to spread corruption among you. Ibn Juzay: 1/159.\nWhat do you think of those who take as advisors or employees enemies of Islam, and what are the consequences of that?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ لَا تَتَّخِذُواْ بِطَانَةٗ مِّن دُونِكُمۡ لَا يَأۡلُونَكُمۡ خَبَالٗا\nA wise person is the one who, when afflicted with the enemy's association, does so only outwardly, and does not reveal anything about his inner self, even if the enemy becomes attached to him and swears that he is one of his allies. Al-Saadi: 144.\nWhen some Muslims have to mix with non-Muslims, what should they do?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ لَا تَتَّخِذُواْ بِطَانَةٗ مِّن دُونِكُمۡ لَا يَأۡلُونَكُمۡ خَبَالٗا وَدُّواْ مَا عَنِتُّمۡ قَدۡ بَدَتِ ٱلۡبَغۡضَآءُ مِنۡ أَفۡوَٰهِهِمۡ وَمَا تُخۡفِي صُدُورُهُمۡ أَكۡبَرُۚ\nThey loved your extreme hardship and harm, and signs of enmity toward you appeared from the slips of their tongues and words, and their hearts concealed much greater hatred than what appears from their mouths because it was a slip of the tongue which rarely happens. Al-Alusi: 4/38.\nAllah forbids taking helpers from among polytheists. Why?\nهَٰٓأَنتُمۡ أُوْلَآءِ تُحِبُّونَهُمۡ وَلَا يُحِبُّونَكُمۡ وَتُؤۡمِنُونَ بِٱلۡكِتَٰبِ كُلِّهِۦ وَإِذَا لَقُوكُمۡ قَالُوٓاْ ءَامَنَّا وَإِذَا خَلَوۡاْ عَضُّواْ عَلَيۡكُمُ ٱلۡأَنَامِلَ مِنَ ٱلۡغَيۡظِۚ قُلۡ مُوتُواْ بِغَيۡظِكُمۡۗ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ عَلِيمُۢ بِذَاتِ ٱلصُّدُورِ ١١٩\nWhat is astonishing is that the believers love the disbelievers while disbelievers actually hate the believers. Ibn Ashur: 4/65.\nThis verse reveals something astonishing. What is it?\nإِن تَمۡسَسۡكُمۡ حَسَنَةٞ تَسُؤۡهُمۡ وَإِن تُصِبۡكُمۡ سَيِّئَةٞ يَفۡرَحُواْ بِهَاۖ\nWhoever has this characteristic of intense enmity, rancor, and joy at the misfortune of the believers is not worthy of being taken as a confidant, especially in the crucial matter of Jihad, which is the basis of goodness in this world and the Hereafter. Al-Qurtubi: 5/281.\nWhat is the wisdom in prohibiting taking disbelievers and hypocrites as confidants, advisors, or employees?\nوَإِن تَصۡبِرُواْ وَتَتَّقُواْ لَا يَضُرُّكُمۡ كَيۡدُهُمۡ شَيۡٔاًۗ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ بِمَا يَعۡمَلُونَ مُحِيطٞ ١٢٠\nPatience includes patience with fate. Fearing Allah includes carrying out His commands and avoiding His prohibitions. Whoever is blessed with both [patience and fear of Allah], attains the best. Unlike the one who does the opposite by disobeying Allah, using fate as an excuse, and losing patience when afflicted, for this is the state of the wretched. .Ibn Taimyah: 2/133.\nDescribe the state of the one whom Allah has granted patience and fear of Him, and another who has been deprived of them.\nوَإِذۡ غَدَوۡتَ مِنۡ أَهۡلِكَ تُبَوِّئُ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ مَقَٰعِدَ لِلۡقِتَالِۗ\nMeaning: You arranged them and placed each in his appropriate place. This is a great praise for the Prophet (r), as he is the one who oversees their placement in the battlefields. This was due to his perfect knowledge, wisdom, foresightedness, and high resolve, as he took care of these matters himself with complete courage, blessings and peace of Allah be upon him. Al-Saadi: 145.\nThe verse contains a praise for the Prophet (r). Explain.\nwords\nلاَ يَألُونَكُم خَبَالًاThey spare no effort to ruin you\nوَدُّوا مَا عَنِتُّمThey wish to see you suffer\nأُولاَءِThey\nغَدَوتَLeft your home in the morning\nتُبَوِّئُTo position"],[66,"§Al-Imran\ndeeds\nTake steps to reconcile two feuding individuals or groups.\nGive a Muslim good news that makes him happy.\nShare a message in which you warn against the risks of usury.\nguid\nThe obligatory gratitude of servants to Allah is manifested in fearing Him by adhering to His commands and avoiding His prohibitions.\nFear Allah and be patient to receive hidden means of His Help.\nBeware of usury and warn others around you against this grave sin.\nrefl\nوَلَقَدۡ نَصَرَكُمُ ٱللَّهُ بِبَدۡرٖ وَأَنتُمۡ أَذِلَّةٞۖ فَٱتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَ لَعَلَّكُمۡ تَشۡكُرُونَ ١٢٣\nAfter mentioning the story of battle of Uhud, Allah mentions the story of battle of Badr when Muslims were few in number and equipment, and the disbelievers were extremely strong and powerful, but Allah granted victory to the Muslims, making this one of the strongest proofs that the fruits of reliance on Allah, patience, and piety is victory, help, and support. Al-Qasimi: 2/402.\nWhy is the story of battle of Badr mentioned after the story of battle of Uhud?\nبَلَىٰٓۚ إِن تَصۡبِرُواْ وَتَتَّقُواْ وَيَأۡتُوكُم مِّن فَوۡرِهِمۡ هَٰذَا يُمۡدِدۡكُمۡ رَبُّكُم بِخَمۡسَةِ ءَالَٰفٖ مِّنَ ٱلۡمَلَٰٓئِكَةِ مُسَوِّمِينَ ١٢٥\nAllah makes clear that by fearing Him and remaining patient, He would send down the angels and give Muslims victory over their enemies. Ibn Taimyah: 2/135.\nFearing Allah and remaining patient are two reasons for the angels to descend to support the believers. Explain.\nوَمَا جَعَلَهُ ٱللَّهُ إِلَّا بُشۡرَىٰ لَكُمۡ وَلِتَطۡمَئِنَّ قُلُوبُكُم بِهِۦۗ وَمَا ٱلنَّصۡرُ إِلَّا مِنۡ عِندِ ٱللَّهِ ٱلۡعَزِيزِ ٱلۡحَكِيمِ ١٢٦\nMeaning: Allah sent down the angels and told you about their descent as glad tidings for you, and to comfort and reassure your hearts. You should know that victory comes only from Allah, and that if He had willed, He could have defeated your enemy without you having to fight them, as He says: (If Allah had willed, He could have subjected them to punishment, but to test some of you by means of others)[47:4]. Ibn Kathir: 1/380.\nDoes Allah need fighters? What do the fighters benefit from being in Jihad?\nوَمَا جَعَلَهُ ٱللَّهُ إِلَّا بُشۡرَىٰ لَكُمۡ وَلِتَطۡمَئِنَّ قُلُوبُكُم بِهِۦۗ وَمَا ٱلنَّصۡرُ إِلَّا مِنۡ عِندِ ٱللَّهِ ٱلۡعَزِيزِ ٱلۡحَكِيمِ ١٢٦\n(Allah ordained this), His promise and support. (Only as glad tidings), so you will be rejoiced by this good news. (To reassure your hearts), to comfort your hearts so that you will not be dismayed by the large number of your enemy. (Victory only comes from Allah, the All-Mighty, the All-Wise), do not attribute victory to the angels and soldiers, as victory comes only from Allah, so seek His help, and entrust all affairs to Him, for glory and judgment belong to Him. Al-Baghawi: 1/415.\nWhat is the only source of victory?\nوَمَا ٱلنَّصۡرُ إِلَّا مِنۡ عِندِ ٱللَّهِ ٱلۡعَزِيزِ ٱلۡحَكِيمِ ١٢٦\nMeaning: Do not rely on the means of victory; rather these means give you some reassurance, but true victory that cannot be overturned comes by the will of Allah; He grants victory to whomever He wills of His servants. If He wills, He will grant victory to those who have the means of attaining victory and are better prepared, as His way with His creation. However, if He wills, He will grant victory to the weaker side to show His servants that the whole matter is in His Hands, and all matters return to Him. Al-Saadi: 146.\nWhat is the benefit in informing Muslims that victory comes solely from Allah?\nلَيۡسَ لَكَ مِنَ ٱلۡأَمۡرِ شَيۡءٌ\nThis verse indicates that the will of Allah prevails over the will of His servants, and that an individual, no matter how high his status, may choose something while the best and most beneficial thing is in another. If the Messenger (r) has no part in the matter, then it is all the more so those who are below him. This is the greatest refutation of those who pin their hopes on Prophets, righteous people and others, and it highlights the fact that doing so is associating others with Allah in worship, and is indicative of a lack of rational thinking, because they turn away from the One Who is in control of all things and turn to those who have no control at all. Al-Saadi: 147.\nFrom this verse, how do you respond to those who cling to Prophets and righteous people beside Allah?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ لَا تَأۡكُلُواْ ٱلرِّبَوٰٓاْ أَضۡعَٰفٗا مُّضَٰعَفَةٗۖ وَٱتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَ لَعَلَّكُمۡ تُفۡلِحُونَ ١٣٠\nMeaning: Shield yourselves from disobeying His prohibition of consuming usury by turning away from worldly things so you may attain your aspirations. For the One Who has the dominion of all existence is able to bestow His favors upon you when you fear Him, and withhold His favors when you neglect His commands. Al-Biqai: 2/152.\nWhat is the link between forbidding usury and commanding the fear of Allah?\nwords\nأَن تَفشَلاَBoth were about to lose courage\nفَورِهِم هَذَاThis hour\nمُسَوِّمِينَThey and their horses were clearly marked\nيَكبِتَهُمDisgrace them with defeat"],[67,"§Al-Imran\ndeeds\nBe the first to do good deeds today, hoping that you will be included in this verse.\nGive to charity whether you are self-sufficient or in need.\nAsk for Allah's forgiveness as many as seventy times throughout your day and night.\nguid\nThe righteous are the people of Paradise, so strive to attain their qualities.\nForgiving people is a virtue.\nDo not be weak or subject yourself to humiliation, as the believer is honorable and victorious with the religion of Islam .\nrefl\nٱلَّذِينَ يُنفِقُونَ فِي ٱلسَّرَّآءِ وَٱلضَّرَّآءِ وَٱلۡكَٰظِمِينَ ٱلۡغَيۡظَ وَٱلۡعَافِينَ عَنِ ٱلنَّاسِۗ وَٱللَّهُ يُحِبُّ ٱلۡمُحۡسِنِينَ ١٣٤\nAfter mentioning the hardest thing to give up and spend, which is money, Allah mentions the hardest thing to withhold, and says, (and who restrain), suppress (their anger) and not release it even after they have been filled with it. Al-Biqai: 2/157.\nWhat is the significance of mentioning suppressing anger after mentioning spending?\nٱلَّذِينَ يُنفِقُونَ فِي ٱلسَّرَّآءِ وَٱلضَّرَّآءِ وَٱلۡكَٰظِمِينَ ٱلۡغَيۡظَ وَٱلۡعَافِينَ عَنِ ٱلنَّاسِۗ وَٱللَّهُ يُحِبُّ ٱلۡمُحۡسِنِينَ ١٣٤\nThe one who restrains his anger and forgives others does kindness to himself as well as to the people, as whoever does good to others is, in fact, does good to himself. Allah says, (If you do good, it is for your own good but if you do evil, it is to your own loss) [17:7]. Ibn Taimyah: 2/140-141.\nWho benefits most from your suppressing your anger and forgiving people? And how?\nوَٱلۡكَٰظِمِينَ ٱلۡغَيۡظَ وَٱلۡعَافِينَ عَنِ ٱلنَّاسِۗ وَٱللَّهُ يُحِبُّ ٱلۡمُحۡسِنِينَ ١٣٤\nMeaning: Those who hold back their anger when their souls are filled with it. It is said: \" So-and-so swallowed his anger,\" if he suppresses it and restrains himself from doing what he is capable of doing. Al-Tabari: 7/214.\nExtract from the verse one of the qualities of those who hasten to forgiveness and Paradise.\nقَدۡ خَلَتۡ مِن قَبۡلِكُمۡ سُنَنٞ فَسِيرُواْ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ فَٱنظُرُواْ كَيۡفَ كَانَ عَٰقِبَةُ ٱلۡمُكَذِّبِينَ ١٣٧\nThis verse highlights the importance of studying history of the people because it is as useful as traveling through the land, which is becoming aware of the stories of ancient people, and the causes of the rise and fall of nations. Ibn Ashur: 4/97.\nReading the history of past nations is important. Explain in light of this verse.\nهَٰذَا بَيَانٞ لِّلنَّاسِ وَهُدٗى وَمَوۡعِظَةٞ لِّلۡمُتَّقِينَ ١٣٨\nThe clear statement is to all who understand it, the guidance and admonition are for the righteous. Ibn Taimyah: 2/143.\nThe clear statement is to all who understand it, the guidance and admonition are only for the righteous. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَلَا تَهِنُواْ وَلَا تَحۡزَنُواْ وَأَنتُمُ ٱلۡأَعۡلَوۡنَ إِن كُنتُم مُّؤۡمِنِينَ ١٣٩\n(Do not weaken) when fighting against your enemies, who are the enemies of Allah, as Allah is with you against them, even when they first overwhelmed you in the battle of Uhud, but you will see who wins at the end. (And do not grieve) over what has befallen you from them, nor over anything else that may befall you, since you (will be superior) in this life and the Hereafter if you are believers. Al-Biqai: 2/159.\nDoes a temporary setback for the believers negate their superiority? Explain.\nوَلَا تَهِنُواْ وَلَا تَحۡزَنُواْ وَأَنتُمُ ٱلۡأَعۡلَوۡنَ إِن كُنتُم مُّؤۡمِنِينَ ١٣٩\nAccording to this verse, peace must not be considered with the enemy as long as the Muslims are strong. If, in a certain country, Muslims lack power, then their Ruler should consider what is best for them. Ibn Atiyah: 1/513.\nWhen is it permissible to make peace with the enemy?\nwords\nالسَّرَّاءِ وَالضَّرَّاءِProsperity and adversity\nوَلاَ تَهِنُواDo not weaken\nقَرحٌA wound\nنُدَاوِلُهَاWe alternate"],[68,"§Al-Imran\ndeeds\nAsk Allah sincerely for martyrdom.\nListen to a lecture or read a book about death.\nRead this verse, then begin defining your life project.\nguid\nTesting, purifying and distinguishing the wicked from the good among people through tribulations is part of Allah's wisdom.\nComfort is achieved through hardship, and bliss is attained through adversity.\nJihad and fighting battles do not advance the death of a servant, and fleeing from Jihad does not delay it either.\nrefl\nوَلَقَدۡ كُنتُمۡ تَمَنَّوۡنَ ٱلۡمَوۡتَ مِن قَبۡلِ أَن تَلۡقَوۡهُ\nThis verse indicates that there is nothing wrong with wishing for martyrdom because Allah approved of their wishes and did not criticize them for that; rather He criticized them for not acting upon their wishes. Al-Saadi: 150.\nIs wishing for martyrdom similar to wishing for death? Explain in light of this verse.\nوَمَا مُحَمَّدٌ إِلَّا رَسُولٞ قَدۡ خَلَتۡ مِن قَبۡلِهِ ٱلرُّسُلُۚ أَفَإِيْن مَّاتَ أَوۡ قُتِلَ ٱنقَلَبۡتُمۡ عَلَىٰٓ أَعۡقَٰبِكُمۡۚ\nThis verse also offers the greatest proof of the virtue of the greatest Siddiq (man of truth), Abu Bakr (t), and the Prophet's Companions who fought the apostates after the death of the Messenger of Allah (r). Al-Saadi: 151.\nFighting the apostates indicates a great understanding and wisdom of Abu Bakr (t) and the Companions. Explain.\nوَمَا مُحَمَّدٌ إِلَّا رَسُولٞ قَدۡ خَلَتۡ مِن قَبۡلِهِ ٱلرُّسُلُۚ أَفَإِيْن مَّاتَ أَوۡ قُتِلَ ٱنقَلَبۡتُمۡ عَلَىٰٓ أَعۡقَٰبِكُمۡۚ\nIn this verse, there is guidance from Allah to His servants that they should be in such a state that their faith cannot be shaken and they should not lose their resolve in adhering to some of its requirements because of the loss of a leader, no matter how great he was. That state can only be attained by making preparations in all matters of their religion by having many qualified people who could step in so that if one is lost, another can take his place. Al-Saadi: 151.\nThis verse provides guidance on an important rule in leadership. Explain\nوَٱللَّهُ يُحِبُّ ٱلصَّٰبِرِينَ ١٤٦ وَمَا كَانَ قَوۡلَهُمۡ إِلَّآ أَن قَالُواْ رَبَّنَا ٱغۡفِرۡ لَنَا ذُنُوبَنَا وَإِسۡرَافَنَا فِيٓ أَمۡرِنَا\nThey combined patience and seeking forgiveness, and this is what is commanded in calamities. Patience with them and seeking forgiveness for the sins that caused them. Ibn Taimyah: 2/156.\nWhat is required in times of calamity?\nوَمَا كَانَ قَوۡلَهُمۡ إِلَّآ أَن قَالُواْ رَبَّنَا ٱغۡفِرۡ لَنَا ذُنُوبَنَا وَإِسۡرَافَنَا فِيٓ أَمۡرِنَا وَثَبِّتۡ أَقۡدَامَنَا وَٱنصُرۡنَا عَلَى ٱلۡقَوۡمِ ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ ١٤٧\nThey realized that sins and excessiveness are among the main reasons to be forsaken by Allah, and that ridding themselves of these sins was one of the main means of attaining victory, so they asked for their Lord's forgiveness. Al-Saadi: 151.\nWhy did the fighters ask forgiveness for their sins and excessiveness?\nوَمَا كَانَ قَوۡلَهُمۡ إِلَّآ أَن قَالُواْ رَبَّنَا ٱغۡفِرۡ لَنَا ذُنُوبَنَا وَإِسۡرَافَنَا فِيٓ أَمۡرِنَا وَثَبِّتۡ أَقۡدَامَنَا وَٱنصُرۡنَا عَلَى ٱلۡقَوۡمِ ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ ١٤٧\nThey sought forgiveness first so that they would be worthy of seeking victory by virtue of their purity from sins over the disbelievers who are surrounded by sins. And in their seeking victory -despite their large numbers- is an indication that they do not look at their numbers, nor do they rely on them, but rather they attribute the firmness of their feet to Allah, and they believe that victory comes from Him, glory be to Him. Al-Alusi: 4/85.\nWhy did they sought forgiveness before asking for victory? Why did they ask for victory despite their large numbers?\nفَـَٔاتَىٰهُمُ ٱللَّهُ ثَوَابَ ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَحُسۡنَ ثَوَابِ ٱلۡأٓخِرَةِۗ وَٱللَّهُ يُحِبُّ ٱلۡمُحۡسِنِينَ ١٤٨\n(So Allah gave them), the One who encompasses knowledge and power. (The reward of this world), He answered their supplication for victory. They became rich with war spoils, had a good reputation, their hearts became reassured and cleared of all evil doubts. Since the reward of this world -whatever it may be- must be tinged with sorrow and accompanied by affliction -because it is the abode of affliction- it is not described as (best), which is only used for: (best reward of the Hereafter). Al-Biqai: 2/164.\nWhy was the reward of the Hereafter described as (best) while this life's reward was not?\nwords\nانقَلَبتُم عَلَى أَعقَابِكُمYou renounced your faith\nرِبِّيُّونَMultitudes of devout men"],[69,"§Al-Imran\ndeeds\nList three aspects of which Muslims imitate the disbelievers, then share them in a message in which you warn against their way of life.\nShare a message in which you warn that viewing wealth is a test of steadfastness in faith and principles, and a cause for discord and conflict dispute among Muslims over the centuries.\nReconcile between two feuding individuals or groups.\nguid\nAssociating partners with Allah is the cause for fear, anxiety and distress in life.\nDo not feel secure from trials and falling into sins, for Allah says about the Companions.\nThe Prophet's Companions (j) had a high status with Allah Who said that He has forgiven them and testified to their faith, which increased the anger of their enemies such as the hypocrites and their followers.\nrefl\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ إِن تُطِيعُواْ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ يَرُدُّوكُمۡ عَلَىٰٓ أَعۡقَٰبِكُمۡ فَتَنقَلِبُواْ خَٰسِرِينَ ١٤٩\nA warning to the believers against following the disbelievers by explaining its harms, calling out to them by describing them as believers, to remind them of a condition that negates that obedience, so that the warning is at its most perfect. Al-Alusi: 4/87.\nWhen warning them against obeying the disbelievers, Allah addresses the believers by saying, (you who believe). Why?\nسَنُلۡقِي فِي قُلُوبِ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ ٱلرُّعۡبَ بِمَآ أَشۡرَكُواْ بِٱللَّهِ مَا لَمۡ يُنَزِّلۡ بِهِۦ سُلۡطَٰنٗاۖ\nIntimidating and terrorizing the disbelievers and hypocrites is from Allah a victory for the believers. Ibn Taimyah:2/157-158.\nThe verse mentions some soldiers of Allah. Explain.\nسَنُلۡقِي فِي قُلُوبِ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ ٱلرُّعۡبَ بِمَآ أَشۡرَكُواْ بِٱللَّهِ مَا لَمۡ يُنَزِّلۡ بِهِۦ سُلۡطَٰنٗاۖ\n(For what they have associated with Allah), the reason for which Allah cast terror into their hearts was because they associated partners with Him. Al-Qurtubi: 5/357.\nExplain how shirk can be a reason for terror and fear.\nحَتَّىٰٓ إِذَا فَشِلۡتُمۡ وَتَنَٰزَعۡتُمۡ فِي ٱلۡأَمۡرِ وَعَصَيۡتُم مِّنۢ بَعۡدِ مَآ أَرَىٰكُم مَّا تُحِبُّونَۚ\n(And disputed over the command), in the battle of Uhud, a dispute arose between the archers, so some of them stood firm as they were commanded while others left their positions. (And disobeyed) you disobeyed the command of the Prophet (r). The address here was directed to all the believers, even though only a small group disobeyed the order, as lesson to all of them, and to hide the identity of those who disobeyed. Ibn Juzay: 1/161.\nWhy was the address directed to all of them, even though only some disobeyed the command?\nحَتَّىٰٓ إِذَا فَشِلۡتُمۡ وَتَنَٰزَعۡتُمۡ فِي ٱلۡأَمۡرِ وَعَصَيۡتُم\nWhen he mentioned losing courage, he followed it up with what is often the cause of it, which is conflict and disobedience. Al-Biqai: 2/168.\nConflict and disobedience are mentioned after losing courage. Why?\nوَلَقَدۡ صَدَقَكُمُ ٱللَّهُ وَعۡدَهُۥٓ إِذۡ تَحُسُّونَهُم بِإِذۡنِهِۦۖ حَتَّىٰٓ إِذَا فَشِلۡتُمۡ وَتَنَٰزَعۡتُمۡ\n(You lost courage), meaning: You became lost and weak by inclining toward the spoils of war, contrary to what high aspirations call for. The Arabs, in their pre-Islamic state, used to boast about their eagerness to stab and strike in battlefields, and their disregard for spoils. Al-Biqai: 2/166.\nFrom the verse, explain what changed the course of the Battle of Uhud from victory for the Muslims to defeat?\nوَٱللَّهُ ذُو فَضۡلٍ عَلَى ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ١٥٢\nBy His grace toward the believers, Allah does not decree for them any blessing or any calamity unless it is ultimately good for them. If something good happens to them, they give thanks, and He grants them the reward of those who are grateful; if something bad happens to them, they endure it with patience and He grants them the reward of those who are patient. Al-Saadi: 152.\nThe verses that mentioned the calamity of the believers conclude with the grace of Allah, the Almighty. Why?\nwords\nتَحُسُّونَهُمSlaying them [enemies]\nتُصعِدُونَFleeing and climbing the mountain\nوَلاَ تَلوُونَWithout looking aside at anyone"],[70,"§Al-Imran\ndeeds\nRemind some of those who are afflicted to have good thoughts about Allah, and that they will eventually realize that He has intended good for them.\nAsk for Allah's forgiveness seventy times today, and ask Him for a good end of your life, since death comes unexpectedly at any time and place.\nYour shortcomings and distance from Allah may be due to a past sin, so give more to charity today, repent and ask for Allah's forgiveness.\nguid\nOne of Allah's ways of honoring His allies is to instill security in their hearts when they need it.\nA sin draws another, and a misdeed leads to another. This is what makes it necessary to repent from the sin immediately.\nSins committed in times of prosperity are a cause of slipping in times of adversity.\nrefl\nثُمَّ أَنزَلَ عَلَيۡكُم مِّنۢ بَعۡدِ ٱلۡغَمِّ أَمَنَةٗ نُّعَاسٗا يَغۡشَىٰ طَآئِفَةٗ مِّنكُمۡۖ\nThey regained their energy and forgot their sorrow, because grief begins to fade after the first sleep that relieves it, as it is seen in the grief of death and other sorrows. Ibn Ashur: 4/133.\nWhat is the benefit of drowsiness descending on the Muslim fighters?\nوَطَآئِفَةٞ قَدۡ أَهَمَّتۡهُمۡ أَنفُسُهُمۡ\nThe hypocrites' aim was not to defend the religion, but rather to save themselves, so they were punished by not gaining the safety and security that was sent upon the believers. Al-Biqai: 2/169.\nThe hypocrites did not feel safe as the believers did. Why?\nقُلۡ إِنَّ ٱلۡأَمۡرَ كُلَّهُۥ لِلَّهِۗ\nMeaning: All victory belongs to Allah, despite the share of His believers since they are His allies. Moreover, it could mean that the decree and destiny belong solely to Allah, and no one else shares in it with Him, so He does what He wills. Al-Alusi: 4/95.\nWhat is the meaning of the Almighty's saying: (All matters belong to Allah)?\nيَقُولُونَ لَوۡ كَانَ لَنَا مِنَ ٱلۡأَمۡرِ شَيۡءٞ مَّا قُتِلۡنَا هَٰهُنَاۗ\nThis is criticism on their part, and disbelief in the will and decree of Allah. It also shows that they regarded the opinion of the Allah's Messenger (r) and that of his Companions as foolish, and that they thought highly of themselves. But Allah responded to them by saying: (Say, \"Even if you had been in your homes\") which were far away from the places of killing, (those among you who were destined to be killed would have come out to their death places). Measures taken to protect oneself -no matter how great they may be- are only of benefit if they are not opposed by the divine will and decree. Al-Saadi: 153.\nWhat the hypocrites said on that day was outrageous. Explain.\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ تَوَلَّوۡاْ مِنكُمۡ يَوۡمَ ٱلۡتَقَى ٱلۡجَمۡعَانِ إِنَّمَا ٱسۡتَزَلَّهُمُ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ بِبَعۡضِ مَا كَسَبُواْۖ\nIn Jihad, fighting depends upon deeds. Whoever is more patient in doing good deeds, will be more steadfast in fighting the disbelievers. Al-Biqai: 2/171.\nIs there a relation between committing sins and deserting Jihad?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ لَا تَكُونُواْ كَٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ وَقَالُواْ لِإِخۡوَٰنِهِمۡ إِذَا ضَرَبُواْ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ أَوۡ كَانُواْ غُزّٗى لَّوۡ كَانُواْ عِندَنَا مَا مَاتُواْ وَمَا قُتِلُواْ لِيَجۡعَلَ ٱللَّهُ ذَٰلِكَ حَسۡرَةٗ فِي قُلُوبِهِمۡۗ\nAllah forbids the believers from thinking the same way as the disbelievers and hypocrites do, which is that whoever travels for trade and the like, or whoever fights and is killed, if he had stayed in his house, he would have lived and not died at the time when he exposed himself to travel or fighting. Ibn Atiyah: 1/530.\nBelief in destiny weakens among the heedless when they hear news of the killing of the mujahideen. Explain this.\nوَلَئِن قُتِلۡتُمۡ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ أَوۡ مُتُّمۡ لَمَغۡفِرَةٞ مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ وَرَحۡمَةٌ خَيۡرٞ مِّمَّا يَجۡمَعُونَ ١٥٧\n(And if you are killed) O believers, in the cause of Allah, that is, in Jihad, or you die a natural death while you are engaged in it by deed or intention (then forgiveness from Allah and mercy is better than what they accumulate) that is, better than all the possessions and worldly pleasures that the disbelievers will have during their lives. This is an encouragement for the believers to engage in Jihad, and that it is something in which competitors must compete. This is also comforting to the believers and a consolation for what befell them in the cause of Allah, after removing any thought that may discourage them from keeping high the word of Allah. Al-Alusi: 4/104.\nWhat is the sign of Allah's good will for the believers? Explain in light of this verse.\nwords\nأَمَنَةًSecurity and safety\nمَضَاجِعِهِمTheir death places\nغُزَّىFighters in the cause of Allah"],[71,"§Al-Imran\ndeeds\nAsk Allah to make you merciful and lenient with your brethren, consult them in some of your matters, and train yourself to have these qualities.\nToday, identify the things that cause you anxiety in your life, then reflect deeply on the attributes of Allah that are appropriate for them to motivate you to rely on Him.\nSet a daily time for reciting the Holy Quran.\nguid\nMercy, forgiveness, humility and gentleness are among the most important qualities of a preacher.\nRemember that seeking victory from someone other than Allah is a defeat. Whoever is helped by Allah is indeed victorious, and whoever is abandoned by Allah is indeed forsaken.\nNever forget that sins and transgressions are the cause of loss, defeat and lack of success.\nrefl\nفَبِمَا رَحۡمَةٖ مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ لِنتَ لَهُمۡۖ وَلَوۡ كُنتَ فَظًّا غَلِيظَ ٱلۡقَلۡبِ لَٱنفَضُّواْ مِنۡ حَوۡلِكَۖ\nPerhaps this mercy from Allah has manifested in the Prophet's (r) calmness during hardship, excellent manners, leniency and gentleness that are attributable to his calmness because whoever controls his anger and emotions, is a completely courageous person. Al-Alusi: 4/105.\nThis verse mentions a sign of Allah's mercy toward the servant. What is it?\nوَشَاوِرۡهُمۡ فِي ٱلۡأَمۡرِۖ\nIt is said that Allah commanded His Prophet (r) to consult with his Companions in order to unite their hearts, set an example to his successors and to bring out their views in matters relating to war tactics that were not part of the revelations by Allah. Therefore, conducting consultation should be even more applicable to those who are below the Prophet (r). Ibn Taimyah: 2/161.\nExplain some of the wisdom behind commanding the Prophet (r) to consult his Companions?\nوَشَاوِرۡهُمۡ فِي ٱلۡأَمۡرِۖ\nThis is an indication that the Prophet's Companions were of high status, had a great insight, and that their insides were pleasing to Allah, the Almighty. Al-Alusi: 4/107.\nThis verse responds to some deviant sects who disregard the Prophet's Companions. Explain.\nفَإِذَا عَزَمۡتَ فَتَوَكَّلۡ عَلَى ٱللَّهِۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يُحِبُّ ٱلۡمُتَوَكِّلِينَ\nPutting trust in Allah (Tawakkul) is: Reliance on Allah to acquire or preserve benefits after they are obtained, and to ward off or remove harm after it has occurred. It is one of the highest levels of faith for two reasons, first: Allah says: (Allah loves those who put their trust in Him). Second: The assurance given in this verse: (Whoever puts his trust in Allah, He is sufficient for him) [65:3]. Ibn Juzay: 1/164.\nWhy is putting trust in Allah considered one of the highest levels of faith?\nإِن يَنصُرۡكُمُ ٱللَّهُ فَلَا غَالِبَ لَكُمۡۖ وَإِن يَخۡذُلۡكُمۡ فَمَن ذَا ٱلَّذِي يَنصُرُكُم مِّنۢ بَعۡدِهِۦۗ\n(But if He forsakes you) and leaves you to your own devices, (then, who is there to help you after Him)? You will inevitably be defeated, even if all people help you. In this, an implicit command to seek Allah's help and rely on Him, and to disavow one's own power and strength. Al-Saadi: 154.\nDoes the help of the powerful replace your reliance and trust in Allah Almighty?\nلَقَدۡ مَنَّ ٱللَّهُ عَلَى ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ إِذۡ بَعَثَ فِيهِمۡ رَسُولٗا مِّنۡ أَنفُسِهِمۡ يَتۡلُواْ عَلَيۡهِمۡ ءَايَٰتِهِۦ وَيُزَكِّيهِمۡ وَيُعَلِّمُهُمُ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ وَٱلۡحِكۡمَةَ\n(Reciting) comes first because it is a prelude. (Purifying) comes next because it is the first thing by which believers acquire a trait. It is considered as a cleansing stage that precedes beautification stage, since warding off harm is more important than bringing about benefits. Then, (teaching) because it is needed only after accepting faith. Al-Alusi: 4/114.\nWhat is the wisdom in mentioning (reciting), (purifying) and (teaching) in this order?\nأَوَلَمَّآ أَصَٰبَتۡكُم مُّصِيبَةٞ قَدۡ أَصَبۡتُم مِّثۡلَيۡهَا قُلۡتُمۡ أَنَّىٰ هَٰذَاۖ قُلۡ هُوَ مِنۡ عِندِ أَنفُسِكُمۡۗ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيۡءٖ قَدِيرٞ ١٦٥\nAllah makes clear that the calamity of the enemy's victory and other things that befell the believers was due to their sins, so He said about the battle of Uhud: (When you suffered a calamity [at Uhud] while you had inflicted twice as much upon them [at Badr], you said, How could this happen? Say, You brought this to yourselves). Ibn Taimyah: 2/167.\nWhat causes calamities for the individual and society?\nwords\nفَظًّاHarsh\nيَغُلَّMisappropriate the spoils of war\nبَاءَHe who incurs"],[72,"§Al-Imran\ndeeds\nWhen you read or hear about a calamity that has befallen Muslims, say:\"There is no might or power except with Allah.\"\nRead a book or listen to a lecture about the virtue of martyrdom in the cause of Allah.\nIdentify three misconceptions about preachers and fighters in the cause of Allah, then respond to them in light of verses from the Quran.\nguid\nBe certain that all the events that take place in the world occur by Allah's knowledge and with His permission, and are based on a great wisdom.\nBeware of those who discourage people from doing good, hooked on worldly life, and seek only their own interests.\nNo fear or grief shall afflict the righteous believer after his death.\nrefl\nوَمَآ أَصَٰبَكُمۡ يَوۡمَ ٱلۡتَقَى ٱلۡجَمۡعَانِ فَبِإِذۡنِ ٱللَّهِ\nAllah says that what befell them of killing and defeat on the day the two armies met, the Muslim army and the polytheist army at Uhud, was by His permission, and in accordance with His will and decree that cannot be avoided and must inevitably come to pass. When the divine decree comes to pass, there is no option but to submit to it and accept it, for there is a great wisdom behind His decree, it brings immense benefits, and it is ordained so that the believer would be distinguished from the hypocrite. Al-Saadi: 156.\nMuslims benefited from their defeat at Uhud. Explain.\nٱلَّذِينَ قَالُواْ لِإِخۡوَٰنِهِمۡ وَقَعَدُواْ لَوۡ أَطَاعُونَا مَا قُتِلُواْۗ قُلۡ فَٱدۡرَءُواْ عَنۡ أَنفُسِكُمُ ٱلۡمَوۡتَ إِن كُنتُمۡ صَٰدِقِينَ ١٦٨\n(Obeyed us) by not going out against Quraysh. (They stayed behind) meaning: They said this statement and sat back themselves from Jihad . Allah responded to them: (Say, then avert death from yourselves) meaning: Say to them, O Muhammad, if you are truthful, then avert death from yourselves. The Arabic word (dar') means ward off. This shows that caution does not avail one against his fate. A person who is killed can only be killed according to his appointed time, and what Allah knows and says will inevitably happen. Al-Qurtubi: 5/405.\nDoes Jihad have an impact on the timing of a person's death?\nوَلَا تَحۡسَبَنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ قُتِلُواْ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ أَمۡوَٰتَۢاۚ بَلۡ أَحۡيَآءٌ عِندَ رَبِّهِمۡ يُرۡزَقُونَ ١٦٩\n(Rather, they are alive) indicates that martyrs are alive and enjoying the provisions of Paradise, unlike the rest of the dead believers who do not enjoy these provisions until they enter Paradise on the Day of Resurrection. Ibn Juzay: 1/166.\nThe martyrs are alive after being killed. Explain.\nوَلَا تَحۡسَبَنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ قُتِلُواْ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ أَمۡوَٰتَۢاۚ بَلۡ أَحۡيَآءٌ عِندَ رَبِّهِمۡ يُرۡزَقُونَ ١٦٩\nThe phrase (with their Lord) is indicative of their high status and their closeness to their Lord (receiving provision) of various kinds of delights that cannot be known or described, except by the One Who bestowed it upon them. Moreover, they are (rejoicing in what Allah has bestowed upon them out of His bounty) that is, they are very happy with it, delighted with it and rejoicing in it. That is because it is beautiful, abundant and great, and there is immense joy when attaining it and there is nothing to spoil that joy. For them, Allah combined the physical joy of the provision and the spiritual joy, with the joy of that which He bestows upon them out of His bounty. Thus, their joy and happiness are complete. Al-Saadi: 156.\nAllah combines for the martyr the bliss of the body and the bliss of the heart and soul. Explain.\nفَرِحِينَ بِمَآ ءَاتَىٰهُمُ ٱللَّهُ مِن فَضۡلِهِۦ وَيَسۡتَبۡشِرُونَ بِٱلَّذِينَ لَمۡ يَلۡحَقُواْ بِهِم مِّنۡ خَلۡفِهِمۡ أَلَّا خَوۡفٌ عَلَيۡهِمۡ وَلَا هُمۡ يَحۡزَنُونَ ١٧٠\nThey lost nothing except the life of distress which no one desires, and they will gain the life of permanent bliss in which no tribulation, sorrow will befall them, nor dismay will touch them on the Day of Gathering. Al-Biqai: 2/180.\nWhat is the reward of those who are killed in the cause of Allah?\nوَيَسۡتَبۡشِرُونَ بِٱلَّذِينَ لَمۡ يَلۡحَقُواْ بِهِم مِّنۡ خَلۡفِهِمۡ أَلَّا خَوۡفٌ عَلَيۡهِمۡ وَلَا هُمۡ يَحۡزَنُونَ ١٧٠\nThey receive good tidings about their brethren, whom they left behind in this life, following the paths of faith and Jihad that they will receive the same great reward when they are martyred. Therefore, the martyrs are rejoiced over this good tidings. Al-Baghawi: 1/448.\nWhy do martyrs receive good tidings about their brethren?\nٱلَّذِينَ قَالَ لَهُمُ ٱلنَّاسُ إِنَّ ٱلنَّاسَ قَدۡ جَمَعُواْ لَكُمۡ فَٱخۡشَوۡهُمۡ فَزَادَهُمۡ إِيمَٰنٗا وَقَالُواْ حَسۡبُنَا ٱللَّهُ وَنِعۡمَ ٱلۡوَكِيلُ ١٧٣\n(Allah is Sufficient for us, and He is the best Protector) these words are the believer's defense against what is feared and hated. These are the same words said by Abraham (u) when he was thrown into the fire. (Allah is Sufficient) He alone is sufficient for us, so we have no fear of anything except Him. (He is the best Protector) this is a praise of Allah and that He is the best refuge from all harms. (So they returned) they returned safe and rewarded. Ibn Juzay: 1/167.\nWhat is the meaning of (Allah is Sufficient for us, and He is the best Protector)?\nwords\nالقَرحُInjuries and pain\nحَسبُنَاIs Sufficient for us"],[73,"§Al-Imran\ndeeds\nConsider three types of luxury and comfort that the disbelieving nations enjoy to understand how Allah gradually lead them to destruction.\nConsider three of satan's ways of tempting and leading people astray.\nHelp someone today with your money, influence, or with anything you can, and remember that Allah, the Almighty, will bless your actions.\nguid\nThe believer's fear of Allah commensurate with his faith in Him.\nBeware of procrastination, as it increases sins, and hasten to repent from all sins.\nOne of the wisdoms behind the commands of Sharia is distinguishing the true believer from the false one.\nrefl\nفَٱنقَلَبُواْ بِنِعۡمَةٖ مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ وَفَضۡلٖ لَّمۡ يَمۡسَسۡهُمۡ سُوٓءٞ وَٱتَّبَعُواْ رِضۡوَٰنَ ٱللَّهِۗ وَٱللَّهُ ذُو فَضۡلٍ عَظِيمٍ ١٧٤\nWhen they entrusted their affairs to Allah and relied with their hearts on Him, He rewarded them with four things: Blessing, favor, averting evil and pursuing His pleasure, and so He was pleased with them as well as they were with Him. Al-Qurtubi: 5/417.\nWhat are the four blessings that the people of faith received when they entrusted their affairs to their Lord, glory be to Him?\nإِنَّمَا ذَٰلِكُمُ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ يُخَوِّفُ أَوۡلِيَآءَهُۥ فَلَا تَخَافُوهُمۡ وَخَافُونِ إِن كُنتُم مُّؤۡمِنِينَ ١٧٥\nThe one who truly fears Allah is the one who fears Allah's punishment, either in this world or in the Hereafter. That is why it is said that the fearful person is not one who weeps and wipes his eyes, but rather the one who abandons sins for which he fears he will be punished. Al-Qurtubi: 5/428.\nWho is the real fearful of Allah, the Almighty?\nإِنَّمَا ذَٰلِكُمُ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ يُخَوِّفُ أَوۡلِيَآءَهُۥ فَلَا تَخَافُوهُمۡ وَخَافُونِ إِن كُنتُم مُّؤۡمِنِينَ ١٧٥\nIf the allies of Allah, the Merciful, remain steadfast in His cause, Allah will reward them with His help and victory over the allies of satan. Whoever fears satan and acts accordingly, will be one of satan's allies. Al-Biqai: 2/185.\nWhat is the description of a person who fears satan and acts according to his fear?\nوَلَا يَحۡزُنكَ ٱلَّذِينَ يُسَٰرِعُونَ فِي ٱلۡكُفۡرِۚ إِنَّهُمۡ لَن يَضُرُّواْ ٱللَّهَ شَيۡٔاًۗ يُرِيدُ ٱللَّهُ أَلَّا يَجۡعَلَ لَهُمۡ حَظّٗا فِي ٱلۡأٓخِرَةِۖ وَلَهُمۡ عَذَابٌ عَظِيمٌ ١٧٦\n(They will never harm Allah at all) the harm caused by disbelievers' actions toward the believers is directed toward Allah and negated. This signifies an honor for the believers where anything that harms them will be as if it harms Allah, the Almighty. Al-Alusi: 4/133.\nThe harm caused by disbelievers' actions toward the believers is directed toward Allah and negated. Why?\nمَّا كَانَ ٱللَّهُ لِيَذَرَ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ عَلَىٰ مَآ أَنتُمۡ عَلَيۡهِ حَتَّىٰ يَمِيزَ ٱلۡخَبِيثَ مِنَ ٱلطَّيِّبِۗ وَمَا كَانَ ٱللَّهُ لِيُطۡلِعَكُمۡ عَلَى ٱلۡغَيۡبِ\nAllah would not let the believers mixed with hypocrites, but He distinguished the two groups from each other by the words and actions that appeared in the Battle of Uhud, indicating either faith or hypocrisy. (Nor would Allah reveal to you the unseen) meaning: Allah would not reveal to you what is in the hearts: faith or hypocrisy. Ibn Juzay: 1/168.\nA great wisdom was revealed to the Muslims through the defeat at Uhud. What is it?\nمَّا كَانَ ٱللَّهُ لِيَذَرَ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ عَلَىٰ مَآ أَنتُمۡ عَلَيۡهِ حَتَّىٰ يَمِيزَ ٱلۡخَبِيثَ مِنَ ٱلطَّيِّبِۗ\n(Until He separates the evil from the good) Allah will expose the falsifier, no matter how long he stays hidden, by difficult burdens and severe conditions, which only the sincere among the servants, who are sincere in belief, can endure. Al-Biqai: 2/187.\nHow does Allah separate the evil from the good?\nوَلِلَّهِ مِيرَٰثُ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِۗ وَٱللَّهُ بِمَا تَعۡمَلُونَ خَبِيرٞ ١٨٠\nAllah states that He is the Everlasting, His Kingdom is eternal and that He will be after time as He was before time, free of any need of the universe. He will inherit the earth after the perishing of His creation and the demise of their kingdoms when there is no one left to claim their wealth. Al-Qurtubi: 5/442.\nDescribe the greatness of Allah as opposed to the insignificance of His creation.\nwords\nفَانقَلَبُواReturned\nنُملِيWe give them respite\nيَجتَبِيHe Selects"],[74,"§Al-Imran\ndeeds\nCommit yourself this day not to say anything unless it is pleasing to Allah, the Almighty, remembering the verse.\nListen to a lecture today, read a story about death, or go visit graves and make it a regular activity for you.\nThink about the life of someone you know who has been severely afflicted, and draw three useful lessons from that.\nguid\nIndeed, Allah is most Forbearing and most Patient with offenses committed by His servants.\nThe most blissful person is one whom Allah spares from the Fire and admits into Paradise.\nIf it is said: (The life of this world), it means: Your ride, house, clothing, your food, and your attempt to be different from others is only the beginning of heedlessness, then delusion and destruction.\nrefl\nسَنَكۡتُبُ مَا قَالُواْ وَقَتۡلَهُمُ ٱلۡأَنۢبِيَآءَ بِغَيۡرِ حَقّٖ وَنَقُولُ ذُوقُواْ عَذَابَ ٱلۡحَرِيقِ ١٨١\nAllah consoled the Prophet (r) by informing him about Messengers who were denied before him, so that he may take them as an example. The death or killing of the Prophet (r) is possible, just as was the case with his fellow Messengers before him. Allah concludes by informing him that many of the Messengers were killed, so death is certain, for no one is immune from death, whether he has a special status or not. . Al-Biqai: 2/192.\nWhat is the wisdom behind informing the Prophet (r) about killing of Prophets before him?\nسَنَكۡتُبُ مَا قَالُواْ وَقَتۡلَهُمُ ٱلۡأَنۢبِيَآءَ بِغَيۡرِ حَقّٖ وَنَقُولُ ذُوقُواْ عَذَابَ ٱلۡحَرِيقِ ١٨١\nThe Jews at the time of the Prophet (r) were satisfied with what their predecessors did by killing the Prophets, and they followed their path of making that permissible and lawful. So, Allah the Most High, attributes the actions of those who followed this path to all of them, as they all belong to the same religion and sect, and were content with each other's actions. Al-Tabari: 7/446.\nWhy is the killing of the Prophets (p) attributed to contemporary Jews, even though the perpetrators were their ancestors?\nوَقَتۡلَهُمُ ٱلۡأَنۢبِيَآءَ بِغَيۡرِ حَقّٖ\n(And their killing the Prophets unjustly) what is meant by describing that action as unjust is that they dared to kill the Prophets, even though they knew it was heinous; nevertheless, they did it out of rebellion and stubbornness, not out of ignorance or misguidance. Al-Saadi: 159.\nAllah describes the Jews' killing of the Prophets as unjust. Why?\nكُلُّ نَفۡسٖ ذَآئِقَةُ ٱلۡمَوۡتِۗ وَإِنَّمَا تُوَفَّوۡنَ أُجُورَكُمۡ يَوۡمَ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِۖ فَمَن زُحۡزِحَ عَنِ ٱلنَّارِ وَأُدۡخِلَ ٱلۡجَنَّةَ فَقَدۡ فَازَۗ وَمَا ٱلۡحَيَوٰةُ ٱلدُّنۡيَآ إِلَّا مَتَٰعُ ٱلۡغُرُورِ ١٨٥\nFor one who is deceived by the enjoyment of delusion, he will certainly regret his actions, while the one who strives to have his death be in the pleasure of his Lord will certainly rejoice. Al-Biqai: 2/193.\nWhat is the sign of a good end of one's life?\nكُلُّ نَفۡسٖ ذَآئِقَةُ ٱلۡمَوۡتِۗ وَإِنَّمَا تُوَفَّوۡنَ أُجُورَكُمۡ يَوۡمَ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِۖ فَمَن زُحۡزِحَ عَنِ ٱلنَّارِ وَأُدۡخِلَ ٱلۡجَنَّةَ فَقَدۡ فَازَۗ\nAllah consoles the Prophet (r) by informing him about Messengers, who were patient and diligent in obedience, until the time of death for them and their nations. They left what was in their hands, unable to defend it, and nothing remained except Allah's kingdom, glory be to Him, the Most High. Both groups await to be recompensed for their deeds; the Messengers of Allah are destined to win, and the disbelievers are destined for the Hellfire. Allah makes clear that this applies to every soul, so that the obedient should strive, and the disobedient should refrain. Al-Biqai: 2/192.\nWhat is the criterion for winning in this life to the believers and to hypocrites?\nلَتُبۡلَوُنَّ فِيٓ أَمۡوَٰلِكُمۡ وَأَنفُسِكُمۡ وَلَتَسۡمَعُنَّ مِنَ ٱلَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ مِن قَبۡلِكُمۡ وَمِنَ ٱلَّذِينَ أَشۡرَكُوٓاْ أَذٗى كَثِيرٗاۚ\nAllah informs the preachers and believers that they will be tested so that they will be ready when it occurs, and face it with patience and steadfastness. The onslaught of calamity increases the hardship, and preparing for distress makes the matter easier. Al-Alusi: 4/147.\nAllah informs the preachers and believers that they will be tested. Why?\nوَإِن تَصۡبِرُواْ وَتَتَّقُواْ فَإِنَّ ذَٰلِكَ مِنۡ عَزۡمِ ٱلۡأُمُورِ ١٨٦\nFearing Allah includes carrying out what is commanded and avoiding what is prohibited. Patience includes being patient with what is decreed by Allah. Ibn Taimyah: 2/185.\nWhat is included in fearing Allah and in patience in this verse?\nwords\nبِقُربَانٍSacrificial offering to Allah\nوَالزُّبُرِEnlightening Scriptures\nزُحزِحَDrawn away"],[75,"§Al-Imran\ndeeds\nToday, look for someone who is ignorant of the rules of performing ablution and prayer, or does not know the short Suras of the Quran and teach him.\nKeep up with your daily remembrance of Allah (Athkar) in the morning, evening and do it while standing, sitting, and lying on your side.\nTonight, look at the sky, the sunrise and the sunset, and reflect on the might of Allah through each one of them.\nguid\nSociety will perish if scholars conceal truth to please people, or to gain wealth, influence or prominence.\nAs an obligation toward his community, a scholar must spread the knowledge he acquired and never conceals any of it .\nBeware of the love of praise and flattery creeping into your heart, or even worse, the love to be praised for what you have not done.\nrefl\nوَإِذۡ أَخَذَ ٱللَّهُ مِيثَٰقَ ٱلَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ لَتُبَيِّنُنَّهُۥ لِلنَّاسِ وَلَا تَكۡتُمُونَهُۥ\nAlhasan and Qatada said: \"This is about everyone who is given knowledge of any part of the Book. Whoever knows something should teach it, and beware of concealing knowledge, for it is an absolute loss.\" Muhammad ibn Ka'b said: \"It is unlawful for a scholar to remain silent about his knowledge or for an ignorant person to remain silent about his ignorance. Allah says, (Allah took a covenant from those who were given the Scripture), and (Ask the people of knowledge, if you do not know)\" [16:43]. Abu Hurairah said: \"If Allah had not taken a covenant from the People of the Scripture, I would not have narrated anything to you.\" Then, he recited this verse: (And when Allah took a covenant from those who were given the Scripture). Al-Qurtubi: 5/458.\nAllah says: (those who were given the Scripture), and does not say, \"taken the Scripture.\" What is the significance and implications of this word?\nٱلَّذِينَ يَذۡكُرُونَ ٱللَّهَ قِيَٰمٗا وَقُعُودٗا وَعَلَىٰ جُنُوبِهِمۡ وَيَتَفَكَّرُونَ فِي خَلۡقِ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِ\nRemembrance of Allah comes before reflection to indicate that the mind alone cannot reach true guidance unless it is enlightened by the remembrance of Allah and His guidance. Therefore, whoever reflects, must return to Allah. Al-Alusi: 4/159.\nThe remembrance of Allah comes before reflection. Why?\nٱلَّذِينَ يَذۡكُرُونَ ٱللَّهَ قِيَٰمٗا وَقُعُودٗا وَعَلَىٰ جُنُوبِهِمۡ\nThis verse indicates that remembrance of Allah should be continuous at all times and in all situations. Al-Baghawi: 1/465.\nWhat is the aim for describing those who remember Allah in these three situations?\nوَيَتَفَكَّرُونَ فِي خَلۡقِ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِ رَبَّنَا مَا خَلَقۡتَ هَٰذَا بَٰطِلٗا سُبۡحَٰنَكَ فَقِنَا عَذَابَ ٱلنَّارِ ١٩١\nUmm Ad-Darda' (i) was asked: \"What was Abu Ad-Darda' (t) occupied with?” She replied: \"He was mostly engaged in reflection.\" Someone said to him: \"Do you consider reflection as a good deed?\" He replied, \"Yes, it is certain faith.\" Ibn Ashur: 4/196.\nThe verse explains a means of reaching certainty. What is it?\nوَيَتَفَكَّرُونَ فِي خَلۡقِ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِ رَبَّنَا مَا خَلَقۡتَ هَٰذَا بَٰطِلٗا سُبۡحَٰنَكَ\nIbn Awn (a prominent scholar) said: Reflection expels heedlessness and causes the heart to fear Allah, just as water causes a plant to grow. Hearts are cleansed by sorrows and enlightened by reflection. Al-Baghawi: 1/465.\nWhat is the importance and benefit of reflection?\nرَبَّنَآ إِنَّكَ مَن تُدۡخِلِ ٱلنَّارَ فَقَدۡ أَخۡزَيۡتَهُۥۖ وَمَا لِلظَّٰلِمِينَ مِنۡ أَنصَارٖ ١٩٢\nAbu Ad-Darda' (t) said: \"May Allah have mercy upon the believers who keep saying: Our Lord, Our Lord, until their prayers are answered.\" Ibn Atiyah: 1/556.\nAccording to Abu Ad-Darda' (t), what is reason for responding to the supplications of the believers?\nرَبَّنَا فَٱغۡفِرۡ لَنَا ذُنُوبَنَا وَكَفِّرۡ عَنَّا سَيِّـَٔاتِنَا وَتَوَفَّنَا مَعَ ٱلۡأَبۡرَارِ ١٩٣\nThey said, (among the righteous) and not \"as righteous\", which means that we are not righteous but gather us with them, and make us their followers. This is an example of humbleness and good manners. Al-Alusi: 4/165.\nThey said: (among the righteous) and not \"as righteous\", Why?\nwords\nوَكَفِّرHide"],[76,"§Al-Imran\ndeeds\nSupplicate Allah, today, with the supplications in these verses, hoping that your supplication will be answered.\nBe more careful today to avoid forbidden looks, fearing Allah, the Almighty, and being patient in avoiding sin.\nChoose beautiful words, or a story about the virtue of patience and its great reward, and share it in a message.\nguid\nDo not be deceived by the disbelievers' superiority and their empowerment in this life, for behind this is wisdom intended by Allah.\nDo not seek worldly gains for memorizing, reflecting and practicing the Quran.\nPatience, perseverance, standing on guard, and fearing Allah are all important to achieve success, which is victory over the enemy in this world, and triumph in the Hereafter.\nrefl\nفَٱلَّذِينَ هَاجَرُواْ وَأُخۡرِجُواْ مِن دِيَٰرِهِمۡ وَأُوذُواْ فِي سَبِيلِي وَقَٰتَلُواْ وَقُتِلُواْ لَأُكَفِّرَنَّ عَنۡهُمۡ سَيِّـَٔاتِهِمۡ وَلَأُدۡخِلَنَّهُمۡ جَنَّٰتٖ تَجۡرِي مِن تَحۡتِهَا ٱلۡأَنۡهَٰرُ\n(Those who migrated) they left the land of polytheism and came to the land of faith, leaving behind their loved ones, brethren, friends and neighbors. (And were driven out of their homes) polytheists tormented them and forced them to migrate. (And suffered for My cause) that is: Their only sin before the people was that they believed in Allah Alone. In similar verse, Allah says, (Their only grievance against them was that they believed in Allah, the All-Mighty, the Praiseworthy) [85:8]. (And who fought and were killed) this is the highest level a Muslim can reach, which is fighting in the cause of Allah. Ibn Kathir: 1/418.\nWhat is the reward for one who migrated, driven out of his home, harmed, or killed in the cause of Allah?\nلَا يَغُرَّنَّكَ تَقَلُّبُ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ فِي ٱلۡبِلَٰدِ ١٩٦\nThis proves that the disbelievers are not blessed in this world, because the reality of blessing is to be free from the taint of both immediate and deferred harm. The blessings of the disbelievers are tainted with pain and punishment. Therefore, it is like someone who is given a sweetness of honey that contains poison. Even if he enjoys eating it, it is not called a blessing because it will eventually kill him. Al-Qurtubi: 5/481.\nAre disbelievers blessed in this life?\nلَا يَغُرَّنَّكَ تَقَلُّبُ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ فِي ٱلۡبِلَٰدِ ١٩٦\nA deceived person is happy with that which he is deceived. The disbelievers are deceived by their prosperity, while the believers are mindful of it. A believer may think that this respite is good for the disbelievers, which may lead him to being deceived by what he sees. That is why the verse begins with: (Do not be deceived). Death is good for both, the believer and the disbeliever. As for the disbeliever, death puts an end to his sins. For the believer, it is because what Allah has is best for the righteous. Ibn Atiyah: 1/558.\nWhy is this word, (deceived), used in the verse?\nنُزُلٗا مِّنۡ عِندِ ٱللَّهِۗ وَمَا عِندَ ٱللَّهِ خَيۡرٞ لِّلۡأَبۡرَارِ ١٩٨\n(For the righteous) meaning: Those who do righteousness, which is the ultimate in piety and good deeds. Some of them said: The righteous are those who do not harm anyone. Ibn Juzay: 1/170.\nWhat is meant by the righteous?\nوَإِنَّ مِنۡ أَهۡلِ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ لَمَن يُؤۡمِنُ بِٱللَّهِ وَمَآ أُنزِلَ إِلَيۡكُمۡ وَمَآ أُنزِلَ إِلَيۡهِمۡ خَٰشِعِينَ لِلَّهِ\nSince their belief was total and real, it became beneficial for them and led them to have fear of Allah that (they do not exchange the verses of Allah for a small price). Hence, they do not give precedence to worldly interests over religious interests, as done by deviant people who conceal what Allah has revealed and exchange it for a small price. These good people have come to know the truth of the matter, and realized that the greatest loss is to settle for what is cheap and inferior, and to give it precedence over religious commitment. Al-Saadi: 162.\nWhat is the sign of true faith?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ ٱصۡبِرُواْ وَصَابِرُواْ وَرَابِطُواْ وَٱتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَ لَعَلَّكُمۡ تُفۡلِحُونَ ٢٠٠\nAllah concludes this Surah with what is included in this tenth verse of the commandment which leads to victory over the enemy in this world and winning the bliss of the Hereafter. Hence, He encourages patience in acts of obedience and in refraining from desires. Patience is restraint. Al-Qurtubi: 5/485.\nThis verse lists few conditions to overcome the enemy and achieve bliss in the Hereafter. What are they?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ ٱصۡبِرُواْ وَصَابِرُواْ وَرَابِطُواْ وَٱتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَ لَعَلَّكُمۡ تُفۡلِحُونَ ٢٠٠\nThis verse indicates the condition for answering supplication for victory over the enemy, and reminds those of understanding to be mindful of Allah, The One, The Living, the All-Sustaining. Al-Biqai: 2/203.\nWhat is the condition for answering supplication for victory over the enemy?\nwords\nتَقَلُّبُProsperity and busy life\nالمِهَادُAbode\nنُزُلًاAccommodation\nوَرَابِطُواStand on guard against your enemy"],[77,"§An-Nisa\ndeeds\nStart making plans today to visit your relatives, and call those who live faraway.\nHelp some orphans in preserving their wealth.\nMake a balance sheet in which you balance the needs of both: This world and the Hereafter.\nguid\nIf one fears that he may not be able to maintain justice between wives, then he should not practice polygamy.\nTreat the orphan's money as you would like people to treat your heirs' money after your death.\nThe presence of a witness at the time of transferring orphans' property back to them is ordained to clear the guardian's responsibility and preserve his reputation.\nrefl\nوَٱتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَ ٱلَّذِي تَسَآءَلُونَ بِهِۦ وَٱلۡأَرۡحَامَۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ كَانَ عَلَيۡكُمۡ رَقِيبٗا ١\nThe believer's awareness of Allah's presence in his life is a noble level of faith. It consists of two parts: Knowledge and state. As for knowledge, it is the believer's knowledge that Allah is aware of him, sees all his deeds, hears all his words, and knows everything that crosses his mind. As for the state, it is the persistence of this knowledge in his heart such that it overcomes it, and he does not lose sight of it. Knowledge without this state is not sufficient. Ibn Juzay: 1/172.\nWhat is the origin of the believer's awareness of Allah's presence in his life?\nوَٱتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَ ٱلَّذِي تَسَآءَلُونَ بِهِۦ وَٱلۡأَرۡحَامَۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ كَانَ عَلَيۡكُمۡ رَقِيبٗا ١\nThe verb (fear) is repeated, because this piety is commanded specifically to Muslims, as there remains among them a remnant of the customs of the Age of Ignorance that they are not aware of, namely carelessness in observing the rights of relatives and orphans. Ibn Ashur: 4/217.\nThe command to fear Allah is repeated twice in this verse. Why?\nوَٱتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَ ٱلَّذِي تَسَآءَلُونَ بِهِۦ وَٱلۡأَرۡحَامَۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ كَانَ عَلَيۡكُمۡ رَقِيبٗا ١\nThere is also another reason to fear Him, which is that you demand your mutual rights in His name, and venerate Him by doing so, in that when you want your needs to be met and your goals fulfilled, you try to get them by asking for them in the name of Allah. Hence, when one wants something from another, he would say to him: I ask you by Allah to do such and such. That is because he knows what the other person has in his heart of veneration toward Allah, which will make him not reject anyone who asks him by Allah. Therefore, just as you venerate Him by doing that, you should also venerate Him by worshiping and fearing Him. Al-Saadi: 163.\nWe venerate Allah in certain things and fail to do so in others. Explain.\nوَءَاتُواْ ٱلۡيَتَٰمَىٰٓ أَمۡوَٰلَهُمۡۖ وَلَا تَتَبَدَّلُواْ ٱلۡخَبِيثَ بِٱلطَّيِّبِۖ\nIn the previous Surah, the story of \"Uhud\" was mentioned, which resulted in orphans, then Allah says, (Every soul will taste death) [3:185], which decrees that death is inevitable, and thus orphans will always be there. Hence, Allah calls for chastity and justice toward them. Fear of Allah is manifested in dealing with orphans who come next to kinships in importance, hence, He says, (And give orphans). Al-Biqai: 2/207.\nAfter mentioning death and the story of \"Uhud\" at the end of Surat Al-Imran, orphans are mentioned in Surat An-Nisa. Why?\nفَٱنكِحُواْ مَا طَابَ لَكُم مِّنَ ٱلنِّسَآءِ مَثۡنَىٰ وَثُلَٰثَ وَرُبَٰعَۖ\nMeaning: Choose as you see fit, and the best of what can be chosen is the quality of religion, as the Prophet (r) said: \"A Woman is married for four reasons: Her wealth, her beauty, her lineage and her religious commitment; choose the one who is religious, may your hands be rubbed with dust.\" This verse indicates that a person should choose before marriage, and it is permissible for him to look at the one he wants to marry in order to be aware of his choice. Al-Saadi: 164.\n(Of your choice) indicates the importance of selecting a wife. Explain.\nفَإِنۡ خِفۡتُمۡ أَلَّا تَعۡدِلُواْ فَوَٰحِدَةً أَوۡ مَا مَلَكَتۡ أَيۡمَٰنُكُمۡۚ\nIn this: One should not put himself in a situation in which he fears injustice, oppression, and failure to fulfill his duty, even if it is permissible. Therefore, he must take the side of caution and protect his religious commitment, for keeping his religious commitment intact is the best. Al-Saadi: 164.\nIf it is likely that injustice will occur, it is wise to avoid its causes. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَلَا تُؤۡتُواْ ٱلسُّفَهَآءَ أَمۡوَٰلَكُمُ ٱلَّتِي جَعَلَ ٱللَّهُ لَكُمۡ قِيَٰمٗا\nThis verse indicates the advantage of having wealth. The righteous predecessors used to say: \"Money is the arm of the believer, and it is better that I leave wealth for which Allah will hold me accountable than living poor and in need of people.\" They used to say: \"Trade and earn money, for you are living in a time when one is in need, he would exchange his religion for it.\" Al-Alusi: 4/202.\nWhat does this verse, (Your property, which Allah has made a means of livelihood for you) refer to?\nwords\nحُوبًاA great sin\nتُقسِطُواMaintain justice\nأَدنَى أَلاَّ تَعُولُواAvoid injustice\nنِحلَةًPerforming a duty graciously\nآنَستُمYou came to know\nوَبِدَارًاHastily\nحَسِيبًاA reckoner and a witness"],[78,"§An-Nisa\ndeeds\nShare a message in which you remind parents of the importance of being fair when dealing with their children.\nStart writing your will today.\nSet a schedule today to pay off your debts, if you have any, before they increase, and seek Allah's Help.\nguid\nThe right of women to inherit is confirmed by the Quran and Sunnah.\nConsuming the wealth of orphans unjustly is extremely prohibited.\nWhoever fears for his children after his death should be kind to other children, for Allah, the Almighty, will reward him with kindness.\nrefl\nلِّلرِّجَالِ نَصِيبٞ مِّمَّا تَرَكَ ٱلۡوَٰلِدَانِ وَٱلۡأَقۡرَبُونَ وَلِلنِّسَآءِ نَصِيبٞ مِّمَّا تَرَكَ ٱلۡوَٰلِدَانِ وَٱلۡأَقۡرَبُونَ مِمَّا قَلَّ مِنْهُ أَوْ كَثُرَ نَصِيبًأ مَّفۡرُوضٗا ٧\nDuring Jahiliya (pre-Islam period), because of their cruelty and hardheartedness, Arabs did not permit the weak, such as women and children, to inherit and they made inheritance for strong men only whom they think that they were able fighters in war and could plunder and seize booty. But the Most Wise, Most Merciful Lord wanted to ordain laws for His servants in which men and women, strong and weak, would be equal. As a precursor to that, He revealed general principles so that people could be acclimated to the idea, then the details came after the general principles had become established, people were prepared to receive it, and they would feel no resentment such as might have stemmed from these abhorrent customs. Al-Saadi: 165.\nHow does the style of the Quran help to change bad ingrained habits?\nوَإِذَا حَضَرَ ٱلۡقِسۡمَةَ أُوْلُواْ ٱلۡقُرۡبَىٰ وَٱلۡيَتَٰمَىٰ وَٱلۡمَسَٰكِينُ فَٱرۡزُقُوهُم مِّنۡهُ وَقُولُواْ لَهُمۡ قَوۡلٗا مَّعۡرُوفٗا ٨\nFrom this, we learn that if anyone shows interest or hopes for some of that which you have in front of you, you should give him something of it. Al-Saadi: 165.\nSharing with others who show interest in what you have is good for both sides. Explain.\nوَإِذَا حَضَرَ ٱلۡقِسۡمَةَ أُوْلُواْ ٱلۡقُرۡبَىٰ وَٱلۡيَتَٰمَىٰ وَٱلۡمَسَٰكِينُ فَٱرۡزُقُوهُم مِّنۡهُ وَقُولُواْ لَهُمۡ قَوۡلٗا مَّعۡرُوفٗا ٨\nThe command is to say to them favorable sayings, that is, kind words -which is opposite of evil- to console some of them for being excluded from the inheritance. Ibn Ashur: 4/252.\nWhy is the command to speak kindly mentioned in this verse?\nوَلۡيَخۡشَ ٱلَّذِينَ لَوۡ تَرَكُواْ مِنۡ خَلۡفِهِمۡ ذُرِّيَّةٗ ضِعَٰفًا خَافُواْ عَلَيۡهِمۡ فَلۡيَتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَ وَلۡيَقُولُواْ قَوۡلٗا سَدِيدًا ٩\nMeaning: let them be just with others now so that Allah will provide just people to deal with their weak offspring after their death. Let them say the right thing now or else, Allah will empower unjust people to oppress their offspring. Al-Biqai: 2/218.\nThe requital befits the action. Explain in light of this verse.\nيُوصِيكُمُ ٱللَّهُ فِيٓ أَوۡلَٰدِكُمۡۖ\nThis shows that Allah is more merciful to His servants than their parents, as He charges parents concerning their children, even though parents usually have total compassion for their children. Al-Saadi: 166.\nHow do you infer from this verse that Allah is more merciful to His servants than their parents?\nمِنۢ بَعۡدِ وَصِيَّةٖ يُوصِي بِهَآ أَوۡ دَيۡنٍۗ\nThe bequest (will) is mentioned before the debt, even though debt has precedence by rule of Sharia, to show the importance of executing the will, as it is likely to be neglected or taken lightly. Al-Alusi: 4/227.\nAllah mentions the will before the debt, even though the debt has precedence by rule of Sharia. Why?\nيُوصِيكُمُ ٱللَّهُ فِيٓ أَوۡلَٰدِكُمۡۖ ... إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ كَانَ عَلِيمًا حَكِيمٗا ١١\nAllah Has ordained these rules perfectly to bring you the most benefit and keep harm away from you. These rules are ordered effectively according to closeness of inheritors to the deceased, such as children and so on. Al-Biqai: 2/221.\nWhat is the significance of mentioning Allah' Names: All-Knowing, All-Wise, at the conclusion of the verses on inheritance?\nwords\nوَسَيَصلَونَThey will enter\nإِخوَةٌTwo or more siblings"],[79,"§An-Nisa\ndeeds\nTake the initiative to write your bequest (will) as the Prophet (r) said:\"It is not right for a Muslim to spend two nights and have something he wants to make a will except to have his will written down at his head.\" [Al-Bukhari & Muslim].\nWhen inheritance rules are applied correctly, they will increase the bond of kinship.\nIf we were left to divide our inheritances, our problems would intensify. Reflect on that, then thank Allah for the blessing of inheritance rules.\nguid\nDue to its impact on the people, Islamic Sharia has set precise rules for the transfer of wealth in all its forms and shapes among them to improves their worldly life.\nWhoever takes lightly the matter of justice among inheritors , Allah will humiliate him on the Day of Resurrection.\nKnow that Allah, the Almighty, has divided the inheritance himself, so it is unlawful for anyone to change it.\nrefl\nوَلَكُمۡ نِصۡفُ مَا تَرَكَ أَزۡوَٰجُكُمۡ\nIbn Al-Qayim said: Think about this meaning from the verse of inheritance, in which Allah makes mutual inheritance conditional upon the word (wives), not \"women\", as He says, (And for you is half of what your wives leave) [4:12], to indicate that this mutual inheritance is only because of being spouses, which is indicative of similarities and of one being part of the other. But there is no similarity between the believer and the disbeliever, and one cannot be part of the other. Therefore, there is no inheritance between them. Al-Saadi: 169.\nIn the inheritance verse, why is the word (wife) used and not \"woman\"?\nمِنۢ بَعۡدِ وَصِيَّةٖ يُوصِي بِهَآ أَوۡ دَيۡنٍۗ مِنۢ بَعۡدِ وَصِيَّةٖ يُوصِينَ بِهَآ أَوۡ دَيۡنٖۚ مِّنۢ بَعۡدِ وَصِيَّةٖ تُوصُونَ بِهَآ أَوۡ دَيۡنٖۗ مِنۢ بَعۡدِ وَصِيَّةٖ يُوصَىٰ بِهَآ أَوۡ دَيۡنٍ\nThe rule of bequest (will) is repeated many times to highlight the importance of respecting and executing the will as is, and not to be neglected or changed by anyone. Al-Biqai: 2/222.\nThe rule of bequest (will) is repeated many times. Why?\nغَيۡرَ مُضَآرّٖۚ وَصِيَّةٗ مِّنَ ٱللَّهِۗ وَٱللَّهُ عَلِيمٌ حَلِيمٞ ١٢\nCausing harm when writing a will is a major sin, including: Bequeathing to an inheritor, bequeathing more than a third of the inheritance or bequeathing a third of the inheritance to harm needy inheritors. Ibn Juzay: 1/179.\nList some of the harms that a will can cause.\nغَيۡرَ مُضَآرّٖۚ وَصِيَّةٗ مِّنَ ٱللَّهِۗ وَٱللَّهُ عَلِيمٌ حَلِيمٞ ١٢\nAllah has ordained that the rights of Muslims take priority over the worldly rights of relatives who are disbelievers. If a Muslim dies, his wealth is transferred to those who are closest to him and most entitled to it. The words of Allah, (And kindred by blood are nearer to one another [regarding inheritance]) are applicable if they are of the same religion, but if they are of different religions, then the brotherhood of faith takes precedence over the brotherhood of blood. Al-Saadi: 169.\nWhich is stronger, religious brotherhood or kinship brotherhood? Explain in light of the rules inheritance.\nيُدۡخِلۡهُ جَنَّٰتٖ تَجۡرِي مِن تَحۡتِهَا ٱلۡأَنۡهَٰرُ خَٰلِدِينَ فِيهَاۚ يُدۡخِلۡهُ نَارًا خَٰلِدٗا فِيهَا\n(They will be abiding therein forever), a plural noun is used to refer to those in Paradise because the people of obedience are the people of intercession, and if one of them intercedes for another, he will enter Paradise with him. (He will be abiding therein forever), a singular noun is used to refer to those in Hellfire because the people of disobedience cannot intercede, so they remain in Hellfire alone. Moreover, eternity in Paradise is in the form of gathering, which is more pleasant, and eternity in Hellfire is in the form of isolation, which is more conducive to loneliness. Al-Alusi: 4/233.\nA plural noun is used to refer to those in Paradise and a singular noun is used to refer to those in Hellfire. Why?\nتِلۡكَ حُدُودُ ٱللَّهِۚ وَمَن يُطِعِ ٱللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُۥ يُدۡخِلۡهُ جَنَّٰتٖ تَجۡرِي مِن تَحۡتِهَا ٱلۡأَنۡهَٰرُ خَٰلِدِينَ فِيهَاۚ وَذَٰلِكَ ٱلۡفَوۡزُ ٱلۡعَظِيمُ ١٣ وَمَن يَعۡصِ ٱللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُۥ وَيَتَعَدَّ حُدُودَهُۥ يُدۡخِلۡهُ نَارًا خَٰلِدٗا فِيهَا وَلَهُۥ عَذَابٞ مُّهِينٞ ١٤\n(And whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger), one who does not increase some of the heirs, nor decrease others by trickery or means, but rather left each one his appointed share as Allah commanded, ordained and divided, (He will admit him to gardens under which rivers flow, abiding therein forever, and that is the great attainment). (And whoever disobeys Allah and His Messenger and transgresses His limits, He will cause him to enter the Fire, abiding therein forever, and for him there will be a humiliating punishment), because he changed what Allah has ordained and opposed His judgment. Ibn Kathir: 1/437.\nThe one who is responsible for dividing the inheritance is subject to either a great promise or a great threat. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَمَن يَعۡصِ ٱللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُۥ وَيَتَعَدَّ حُدُودَهُۥ يُدۡخِلۡهُ نَارًا خَٰلِدٗا فِيهَا\nThe one who combines disobedience and obedience will be subject to reward and punishment commensurate with the extent of his obedience and disobedience. Authentic Sharia texts indicate that those who are obedient with regard to belief in the Oneness of Allah will not abide forever in Hellfire because their belief in the Oneness of Allah will prevent them from abiding therein forever. Al-Saadi: 169.\nWhat is the virtue of the belief in the Oneness of Allah (Tawhīd)?\nwords\nوَلَدٌA son or a daughter\nكَلاَلَةًOne who has no descendants nor ascendants"],[80,"§An-Nisa\ndeeds\nAsk for Allah's forgiveness and repent to Him as many as seventy times while remembering your sins and errs.\nConsider those who died while living in sin; this may be a reminder to you from your Lord, then hasten to repent and reform your way of life.\nRepel devilish whispers about your wife or sister by seeking refuge with Allah and blowing your breath over to your left side.\nguid\nRepentance is more beneficial when it occurs soon after the sin.\nBeware of injustice, especially against those who are weak, such as women, for Allah will support every weak person, so beware of His punishment.\nA man must treat his wife with kindness, good company, refrain from harming her, be kind, and treat her well. This includes providing maintenance and clothing.\nrefl\nوَٱلَّٰتِي يَأۡتِينَ ٱلۡفَٰحِشَةَ مِن نِّسَآئِكُمۡ فَٱسۡتَشۡهِدُواْ عَلَيۡهِنَّ أَرۡبَعَةٗ مِّنكُمۡۖ\nIt was said that requiring four witnesses for adultery in order to make it tougher for the accuser and to protect the dignity of people. Ibn Juzay: 1/179.\nFour witnesses are required to prove adultery. Why?\nوَٱلَّٰتِي يَأۡتِينَ ٱلۡفَٰحِشَةَ مِن نِّسَآئِكُمۡ\nThis refers to women who (commit immoral conduct) namely adultery, which is described as immoral conduct because of its abhorrent nature. Al-Saadi: 171.\nWhy is adultery described as immoral conduct?\nإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ كَانَ تَوَّابٗا رَّحِيمًا ١٦\n(Most Merciful), Allah chooses whomever He wills of His servants to do what He is pleased with. Hence, deal with sinners who repent like He does, be merciful to them when they repent, and when admonishing them, use kind words to soften their hearts. Al-Biqai: 2/226.\nThe verse concludes with Allah's holy names: (Accepting of Repentance) and (Most Merciful). What is the significance of that?\nإِنَّمَا ٱلتَّوۡبَةُ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ لِلَّذِينَ يَعۡمَلُونَ ٱلسُّوٓءَ بِجَهَٰلَةٖ\nMeaning: One who is ignorant of the consequences of his sin and does not know that it will incur the wrath and punishment of Allah. He is also unaware that Allah is constantly watching him, and he does not know that his sin will lead to diminishing or erasing his faith. Everyone who disobeys Allah is ignorant in this sense, even if he is knows that it is forbidden. Al-Saadi: 171.\nWhat is the true meaning of the ignorance of a sinner?\nوَعَاشِرُوهُنَّ بِٱلۡمَعۡرُوفِۚ\nThis is addressed to all, as everyone has company of women, whether they are husbands or guardians. The command, however, is directed particularly to husbands, as Allah says, (then either retaining in all kindness) which means fulfilling her right in terms of dowry and maintenance, not frowning at her for no reason, and being cheerful in speech, not rude, nor harsh, nor showing a tendency to favor others. Al-Qurtubi: 6/159.\nHow is living with women in kindness achieved?\nفَإِن كَرِهۡتُمُوهُنَّ فَعَسَىٰٓ أَن تَكۡرَهُواْ شَيۡـٔٗا وَيَجۡعَلَ ٱللَّهُ فِيهِ خَيۡرٗا كَثِيرٗا ١٩\nMeaning: You -the husbands- should keep your wives even if you dislike them, for there is a great deal of good in that, such as obeying Allah's command and accepting His advice, which leads to happiness in this world and the Hereafter. Therefore, the husband should exert himself -even if he does not love her- to develop a good attitude so that he can treat her kindly; perhaps his dislike of her will disappear, and be replaced by love, as it usually happens; or perhaps Allah will bless him with a righteous child from her, who will benefit his (or her) parents in this world and the Hereafter. Al-Saadi: 172.\nWhat are the benefits of keeping a wife whom her husband does not like?\nفَعَسَىٰٓ أَن تَكۡرَهُواْ شَيۡـٔٗا وَيَجۡعَلَ ٱللَّهُ فِيهِ خَيۡرٗا كَثِيرٗا ١٩\nIf you dislike them, then be patient and do not leave them based on feelings only, for you may find much good in what you dislike. The soul may dislike what is good and love that which is not, therefore, let your judgment be based on what is good and right, not what the soul desires. Al-Alusi: 4/234.\nWhat are the consequences of following one's desires in everything?\nwords\nبِجَهَالَةٍOut of ignorance and foolishness\nمِن قَرِيبٍBefore the time of death\nتَعضُلُوهُنَّDo not hold on to them in marriage forcibly"],[81,"§An-Nisa\ndeeds\nWrite down the amount of dowry of the Prophet's (r) daughters and share it in a message.\nList all the weak people whose rights Allah defends in Surat An-Nisa, and share them in a message to endear people to their Creator.\nList three of Sharia's rulings that are enacted to preserve the ties among kinships so that you realize its importance to Allah.\nguid\nStrict prohibition of taking back the dowry deters those who take divorce lightly.\nIt is an obligation to keep, honor and respect all covenants.\nSharia has taken care to preserve kinships ties by forbidding Muslims from marrying two sisters simultaneously.\nrefl\nوَإِنۡ أَرَدتُّمُ ٱسۡتِبۡدَالَ زَوۡجٖ مَّكَانَ زَوۡجٖ وَءَاتَيۡتُمۡ إِحۡدَىٰهُنَّ قِنطَارٗا\nIt is better and more appropriate to follow the example of the Prophet (r) in giving a moderate dowry. Al-Saadi: 173.\nWhat is the best approach when deciding the amount for dowry?\nوَإِنۡ أَرَدتُّمُ ٱسۡتِبۡدَالَ زَوۡجٖ مَّكَانَ زَوۡجٖ وَءَاتَيۡتُمۡ إِحۡدَىٰهُنَّ قِنطَارٗا فَلَا تَأۡخُذُواْ مِنۡهُ شَيۡـًٔاۚ أَتَأۡخُذُونَهُۥ بُهۡتَٰنٗا وَإِثۡمٗا مُّبِينٗا ٢٠\nTaking back the dowry from the wife is called (injustice) because it was their custom in the past, when one hated his wife and wanted to divorce her, he would accuse her of bad partnership and other unfounded charges so that she becomes fearful for her reputation and agrees to pay him money to divorce her. Ibn Ashur: 4/289.\nWhy is taking the dowry that the husband paid to his wife called (injustice) in this verse?\nوَكَيۡفَ تَأۡخُذُونَهُۥ وَقَدۡ أَفۡضَىٰ بَعۡضُكُمۡ إِلَىٰ بَعۡضٖ وَأَخَذۡنَ مِنكُم مِّيثَٰقًا غَلِيظٗا ٢١\nThe solemn covenant that is taken by wives from their husbands is keeping in all kindness, or releasing with good treatment. Al-Tabari: 8/127.\nWhat is the solemn covenant that wives took from their husbands?\nوَكَيۡفَ تَأۡخُذُونَهُۥ وَقَدۡ أَفۡضَىٰ بَعۡضُكُمۡ إِلَىٰ بَعۡضٖ وَأَخَذۡنَ مِنكُم مِّيثَٰقًا غَلِيظٗا ٢١\nSince the previous verse dealt with the ruling of divorce caused by the wife, and therefore the husband is entitled to take money back from her, Allah follows that by mentioning the divorce caused by the husband, and that if the husband wants a divorce that is not caused by disobedience or bad treatment by the wife, then he does not have the right to ask her for money. Al-Qurtubi: 6/170.\nWhen is it prohibited for the husband to ask for money to divorce his wife?\nوَلَا تَنكِحُواْ مَا نَكَحَ ءَابَآؤُكُم مِّنَ ٱلنِّسَآءِ إِلَّا مَا قَدۡ سَلَفَۚ إِنَّهُۥ كَانَ فَٰحِشَةٗ وَمَقۡتٗا وَسَآءَ سَبِيلًا ٢٢\nImmorality includes immoral contracts as well as immoral acts. Ibn Taimyah: 2/222.\nImmorality includes immoral contracts as well as immoral acts. How?\nحُرِّمَتۡ عَلَيۡكُمۡ أُمَّهَٰتُكُمۡ وَبَنَاتُكُمۡ وَأَخَوَٰتُكُمۡ وَعَمَّٰتُكُمۡ وَخَٰلَٰتُكُمۡ\nThis list of prohibited women for a person to marry is attributed to a noble principle of preserving the honor of these women, which is one of the earliest manifestations of human progress. Ibn Ashur: 4/289.\nWhy are these women prohibited for a person to marry?\nوَأَن تَجۡمَعُواْ بَيۡنَ ٱلۡأُخۡتَيۡنِ إِلَّا مَا قَدۡ سَلَفَۗ\nAllah mentions the case of one who is married to two sisters simultaneously and forbade it. That is because this will be a cause of severing ties of kinships. Al-Saadi: 174.\nWhy is it prohibited for a person to be married to two sisters simultaneously?\nwords\nقِنطَارًاA great amount of money\nبُهتَانًاInjustice\nأَفضَىBeen intimate\nوَرَبَائِبُكُمُYour step-daughters\nوَحَلاَئِلُWives"],[82,"§An-Nisa\ndeeds\nDisseminate the concepts of modesty, chastity, and proper hijab for Muslim women using available means.\nAsk Allah to grant you patience and guide you to attain it.\nNo matter how sinful you think you are, always ask Allah for forgiveness and repent to Him, remembering that He wants to accept your His servants' repentance and loves that, therefore, expect the best from Him.\nguid\nDealing with people should be based on what they display; it is not the duty of the believer to track what is hidden.\nRighteousness, reason, and chastity are essential qualities when choosing a wife, and they take precedence over other qualities.\nThere is much good in patience.\nrefl\nوَأُحِلَّ لَكُم مَّا وَرَآءَ ذَٰلِكُمۡ\nAll those who are not mentioned in this verse are permissible and good. Thus, what is prohibited is limited, but there is no limit or restriction on what is permitted. This is the kindness and mercy of Allah to make things easy for people. Al-Saadi: 174.\nThis verse indicates the ease of this religion and the vastness of Allah's mercy. Explain.\nوَٱللَّهُ أَعۡلَمُ بِإِيمَٰنِكُمۚ بَعۡضُكُم مِّنۢ بَعۡضٖۚ\nDo not judge the faith of others by speculating that which in their hearts, rather be content with their outward display of faith, for only Allah Knows best about your faith. Al-Baghawi: 1/509.\nIs judging others by speculating what is in their hearts a good Muslim approach? Why?\nذَٰلِكَ لِمَنۡ خَشِيَ ٱلۡعَنَتَ مِنكُمۡۚ وَأَن تَصۡبِرُواْ خَيۡرٞ لَّكُمۡۗ وَٱللَّهُ غَفُورٞ رَّحِيمٞ ٢٥\nThe Arabic word \"Al-Anat\", which means (falling into sin), originally comes from an Arabic literal meaning: \"The fracture of a bone after it has been mended.\" It is used as a metaphor for every hardship and harm that befalls a person after his condition has condition has improved, and there is no greater harm than committing the most heinous of sins by someone after he reformed himself. Al-Alusi: 5/12.\nMarrying a slave-woman because of fearing \"Al-Anat.\" Explain.\nفَإِنۡ أَتَيۡنَ بِفَٰحِشَةٖ فَعَلَيۡهِنَّ نِصۡفُ مَا عَلَى ٱلۡمُحۡصَنَٰتِ مِنَ ٱلۡعَذَابِۚ ذَٰلِكَ لِمَنۡ خَشِيَ ٱلۡعَنَتَ مِنكُمۡۚ وَأَن تَصۡبِرُواْ خَيۡرٞ لَّكُمۡۗ وَٱللَّهُ غَفُورٞ رَّحِيمٞ ٢٥\nThis verse concludes with these two noble Names of Allah: (All-Forgiving) and (Most Merciful), because these rulings are a mercy and kindness to people. Allah did not place constraints on them; rather He has given them a great latitude in these rulings. Mentioning forgiveness after the mention of Hadd (a mandatory prescribed penalty) indicates that Hadd penalties are expiation by means of which Allah forgives the sins of His servants as it is stated in a Prophetic Hadith. Al-Saadi: 175.\nThe verse concludes with two Names of Allah: (All-Forgiving) and (Most Merciful). Why?\nيُرِيدُ ٱللَّهُ لِيُبَيِّنَ لَكُمۡ وَيَهۡدِيَكُمۡ سُنَنَ ٱلَّذِينَ مِن قَبۡلِكُمۡ\n(To make things clear to you), meaning: To make clear to you the matter of your religion, the interests of your affair, and what is permissible for you and what is forbidden to you. This indicates that nothing is left without guidance from Allah as He says: (We left nothing unaccounted for in the Book) [6:38]. Al-Qurtubi: 6/244.\nIs there an emerging issue or a contemporary case in which Allah's Sharia does not have a statement or ruling?\nيُرِيدُ ٱللَّهُ لِيُبَيِّنَ لَكُمۡ وَيَهۡدِيَكُمۡ سُنَنَ ٱلَّذِينَ مِن قَبۡلِكُمۡ\nMeaning: Allah guides you to the ways of the Prophets and righteous people before you, so that you can follow their example. Ibn Juzay: 1/186.\nThroughout the years, the believers have been brothers who follow each other's example. Explain in light of this verse.\nيُرِيدُ ٱللَّهُ لِيُبَيِّنَ لَكُمۡ وَيَهۡدِيَكُمۡ سُنَنَ ٱلَّذِينَ مِن قَبۡلِكُمۡ وَيَتُوبَ عَلَيۡكُمۡۗ وَٱللَّهُ عَلِيمٌ حَكِيمٞ ٢٦\n(And accept your repentance), Meaning: Allah shows mercy to you in all your situations and in all that which He prescribes for you, so that you will be aware of the limits of Allah and be content with what He has permitted; then your sins will be lessened because of what Allah has made easy for you. This is from His mercy toward His servants. Moreover, from His mercy toward them is that if they commit a sin, He opens the gates of mercy to them and directs their hearts to repent to Him, and humble themselves before Him, then He accepts their repentance of that which He guided them to. Al-Saadi: 175.\nHow does Allah accept His servants' repentance?\nwords\nوَالمُحصَنَاتُMarried women\nمُحصِنِينَBeing chaste\nمُسَافِحِينَBeing adulterers\nطَولًاFinancial capacity\nمُتَّخِذَاتِHaving secret paramours\nالعَنَتَFalling into sin"],[83,"§An-Nisa\ndeeds\nWorship Allah by making a piece for the media (a message, an article, a visual presentation, a poem) in which you warn against following lusts that are spread by corruptors in the country.\nHumble yourself to Allah, acknowledging your weakness and helplessness, for Allah is with those whose hearts are submissive to Him.\nAvoid being in a place that reminds you of a major sin and ask often for Allah's forgiveness.\nguid\nA person afflicted with forbidden desires wants all people to be like him, just as a pure person desires all people to be pure..\nThere is no human being who is not tested by Allah with two types of preachers: Preachers of good and preachers of evil.\nProperty of others are forbidden to you except by lawful means and with their consent, so avoid consuming forbidden money.\nrefl\nوَٱللَّهُ يُرِيدُ أَن يَتُوبَ عَلَيۡكُمۡ وَيُرِيدُ ٱلَّذِينَ يَتَّبِعُونَ ٱلشَّهَوَٰتِ أَن تَمِيلُواْ مَيۡلًا عَظِيمٗا ٢٧\nOnce you realize that Allah enjoins upon you what is in your best interests, and will lead to your success and happiness, while those who follow their whims and desires are enjoining upon you that which will lead to the utmost loss and misery, then choose for yourselves the better of the two callers, and select the better of the two path. Al-Saadi: 175.\nAllah clarifies the paths for people, so what should they do?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ لَا تَأۡكُلُوٓاْ أَمۡوَٰلَكُم بَيۡنَكُم بِٱلۡبَٰطِلِ ... وَلَا تَتَمَنَّوۡاْ مَا فَضَّلَ ٱللَّهُ بِهِۦ بَعۡضَكُمۡ عَلَىٰ بَعۡضٖۚ\nWhen Allah forbade consuming people's property unlawfully and killing oneself, He warned against the consequences of greed for people’s property, either by physically taking some of it, or by envying them for what they own. This is to ensure that their outward and inward deeds are pure. Al-Alusi: 5/19.\nDesiring the blessings of others is prohibited. Why?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ لَا تَأۡكُلُوٓاْ أَمۡوَٰلَكُم بَيۡنَكُم بِٱلۡبَٰطِلِ إِلَّآ أَن تَكُونَ تِجَٰرَةً عَن تَرَاضٖ مِّنكُمۡۚ\nThis verse is the best proof against some ignorant Sufis who disapprove of making a living through trade and manufacturing. Al-Qurtubi: 6/250.\nDoes striving to seek a livelihood and trade contradict reliance upon Allah? Explain in light of this verse.\nإِن تَجۡتَنِبُواْ كَبَآئِرَ مَا تُنۡهَوۡنَ عَنۡهُ نُكَفِّرۡ عَنكُمۡ سَيِّـَٔاتِكُمۡ وَنُدۡخِلۡكُم مُّدۡخَلٗا كَرِيمٗا ٣١\nIbn Abbas (t) said: Major sins are every sin that Allah mentions its punishment as Hellfire, curse or wrath. Ibn Juzay: 1/187.\nWhat is meant by \"major sins\"? Give three examples.\nوَلَا تَتَمَنَّوۡاْ مَا فَضَّلَ ٱللَّهُ بِهِۦ بَعۡضَكُمۡ عَلَىٰ بَعۡضٖۚ لِّلرِّجَالِ نَصِيبٞ مِّمَّا ٱكۡتَسَبُواْۖ وَلِلنِّسَآءِ نَصِيبٞ مِّمَّا ٱكۡتَسَبۡنَۚ وَسۡـَٔلُواْ ٱللَّهَ مِن فَضۡلِهِۦٓۚ\nThe reason of revelation of this verse (Do not wish...) is that women said: \"If only we were equal to men in inheritance and participated with them in Jihad.\" So, this verse was revealed forbidding them from wishing that because it implies a rejection of the rules of Sharia. This prohibition, also, includes wishing things that are against the rules of Sharia. Ibn Juzay: 1/187.\nWishing for what Allah has favored some people over others is prohibited. Why?\nوَلَا تَتَمَنَّوۡاْ مَا فَضَّلَ ٱللَّهُ بِهِۦ بَعۡضَكُمۡ عَلَىٰ بَعۡضٖۚ\nAllah forbade wishing for what He has bestowed upon others because it leads to envy. Envy is when a person wishes for the loss of a blessings from another, whether he wishes it for himself or not, and this is forbidden. However, aspiration is when one wishes to have the same possessions or qualities, then it is permissible. Al-Kalbi (a prominent scholar) said: \"One should not wish for another man's wealth, wife or servant, but he should say, \"O Allah grant me similar to what he has.\" Al-Baghawi: 1/517.\nWhat is the difference between envy and aspiration?\nلِّلرِّجَالِ نَصِيبٞ مِّمَّا ٱكۡتَسَبُواْۖ وَلِلنِّسَآءِ نَصِيبٞ مِّمَّا ٱكۡتَسَبۡنَۚ\nIn this verse, the favors of Allah upon both men and women are expressed as rewards of their deeds, affirming the entitlement of each to his/her share so that it does not pass over to others. This should end the wishing, as each has a share of reward according to what Allah Almighty has charged him with of acts of obedience through His good governance. Al-Alusi: 5/19.\nWhy are the favors of Allah upon men and women expressed as rewards of their deeds?\nwords\nكَبَائِرَMajor sins\nسَيِّئَاتِكُمMinor sins\nمَوَالِيَHeirs\nوَالَّذِينَ عَقَدَت أَيمَانُكُمThose to whom you have made a pledge"]])